PVD("japan_ndp_2026-2026",{"docs":["","JPN Honebuto 2026 Japanese"],"s":{"1":[[1,"16","2","Regional Minimum Wage Disparity Reduction","Efforts will be made to correct regional disparities, including by raising the ratio of the lowest regional minimum wage to the highest.",""],[1,"10","7","Strategy to Strengthen Small and Mid-Sized Enterprise Earning Power","“Strategy to Strengthen the Earning Power of Mid-sized and Small Enterprises in a Labor Supply-Constrained Society”",""],[1,"15","5","Labor Productivity Improvement for Minimum Wage Growth","The public and private sectors will continue making tireless efforts and promote continuous improvements in labor productivity.",""],[1,"16","1","SME Productivity Improvement Support","Sufficiently support efforts by prefectures and municipalities to improve the productivity of small and medium-sized enterprises using grants and other means.",""],[1,"16","2","Data-Based Annual Minimum Wage Determination","The Central Minimum Wage Council and Local Minimum Wage Councils, composed of representatives of the public, labor, and management, will deliberate and decide on annual minimum wage increases based on data on the three statutory factors and actual conditions.",""],[1,"15","7","Acceleration Plan for Price Pass-Through and Fair Transactions in Government Procurement","Under the Acceleration Plan for Price Pass-Through and Fair Transactions in Government Procurement, implement the preparation of planned prices based on actual market prices and the introduction and application of low bid price investigation systems or minimum limit price systems at 100% by the end of fiscal year 2027.",""]],"3":[[1,"19","5","Public Service Recruitment Strengthening","Recruitment activities will be broadly strengthened.",""],[1,"19","5","Public Service Workplace Environment Improvement","The workplace environment will be developed to compete with that of private companies and other organizations.",""],[1,"19","5","Public Service Talent Management Strengthening","Talent management will be strengthened.",""],[1,"19","5","Advanced Public Personnel Management Functions","Personnel management functions will be upgraded.",""],[1,"19","5","Public Servant Employment Conditions Improvement","Employment conditions will be improved.",""]],"6":[[1,"33","3","Medical Informatization Promotion Policy","Formulate a policy to promote medical informatization",""],[1,"33","3","Healthcare Information System Renewal","Promote the renewal of information systems in medical institutions",""],[1,"33","3","Healthcare Cybersecurity Measures","Advance cybersecurity measures, including urgent responses for advanced treatment hospitals and other institutions",""],[1,"33","3","Electronic Medical Record and Prescription Diffusion","Promote the widespread adoption of electronic medical records and electronic prescriptions",""],[1,"34","1","Healthcare and Long-Term Care Data Utilization Infrastructure","Construct a foundation for the linkage and secondary use of information on medical care and nursing care, including databases for medicines and the digitization of publicly funded medical care, vaccinations, and maternal and child health, to provide seamless and optimal services efficiently.",""],[1,"34","7","Genomic Information Platform Development and Data Utilization","The Japan Genome Medicine Promotion Organization (GeMJ) will develop a high-quality genomic information platform containing whole-genome data, multi-omics data, clinical information, and other data, and promote the utilization of analytical data.",""]],"8":[[1,"11","6","Automated Driving Enabling Environment Development","Develop an environment for the early realization of an automated driving society that responds to technological innovation.",""],[1,"12","3","Safe Autonomous Driving and Ride-Sharing Measures","To address the shortage of mobility options nationwide, advance necessary measures concerning autonomous driving and ride-sharing based on examples from other countries and the needs of each region, subject to ensuring safety and security and appropriate working conditions.",""],[1,"12","3","Autonomous Driving Legislative Review","Work specifically on reviewing relevant laws and regulations in response to the characteristics of autonomous driving.",""],[1,"13","4","Mobility Infrastructure and Energy Conservation Promotion","Promote the use of mobility infrastructure and energy conservation.",""]],"14":[[1,"13","4","Energy Supply-Demand Resilience Policy","Strengthen the resilience of the energy supply-demand structure, including stockpiling.",""],[1,"13","4","Domestic Oil Upstream Rights Acquisition","Secure upstream rights for oil and other resources held by Japan.",""],[1,"13","4","Energy Supply Source Diversification Policy","Diversify supply sources.",""],[1,"13","4","Stable Energy Transport and Distribution System","Ensure a stable transport and distribution system.",""],[1,"14","1","Asia Energy and Resources Supply Resilience Partnership","Through the Asia Energy and Resources Supply Resilience Partnership (Power Asia), further evolving economic and energy resilience through cooperation with Asian countries and others.",""],[1,"14","2","Critical Minerals Supply Diversification Support","Support the diversification of supply sources for critical minerals.",""],[1,"14","2","National Critical Minerals Stockpile Strengthening","Strengthen national stockpiles.",""],[1,"14","2","Marine Resource Security Development","Accelerate efforts to secure marine resources, including seabed rare-earth resources around Minamitorishima.",""],[1,"14","2","Metal Recycling Promotion Strategy","Through the Metal Recycling Promotion Strategy and other measures based on the Circular Economy Action Plan, promote metal recycling.",""],[1,"14","2","Recycled Resources Supply Chain Strengthening","Strengthen the resilience of supply chains for recycled resources.",""],[1,"41","5","Crude Oil Supply Stabilization Measures","In response to the current situation in the Middle East, stable crude oil supply will be secured through alternative procurement and, when necessary, the release of stockpiles.",""],[1,"41","5","Critical Goods Supply and Distribution Measures","Efforts will also be made to secure the stable supply of critical goods and ensure smooth distribution.",""]],"17":[[1,"37","4","Science, Technology and Innovation Basic Plan","Steadily promote the newly formulated Basic Plan for Science, Technology and Innovation.",""],[1,"37","4","Evidence-Based Science Policy Strengthening","Strengthen EBPM for science and technology policy.",""],[1,"37","4","National University Research Funding Expansion","Significantly expand National University Corporation Management Expense Grants and Grants-in-Aid for Scientific Research to stably and continuously support research activities at universities.",""],[1,"37","4","Planned Research Facility Development Support","Provide steady support for the planned development of facilities.",""],[1,"37","4","Science and Technology Research Foundation Strengthening","Strengthen the foundation for science and technology research, including basic research.",""],[1,"37","4","International Researcher Mobility Hub Development","Make Japan a major hub for the international circulation of talent.",""],[1,"37","5","National Institute of Technology Operating Grant","This includes steadily securing operating grants for the National Institute of Technology Organization.",""],[1,"38","1","National Research Institute Operating Grant Expansion","At the same time, efforts will be made to strengthen the research and development foundations of national research institutes through the expansion of operating grants and other measures.",""],[1,"38","1","Moonshot Research and Development Programme","In addition, support for important technology areas will be enhanced through the promotion of Moonshot-type research and development (challenging research and development based on bolder ideas).",""],[1,"38","2","Full Fund-Based Research Grants Mechanism","Promote efforts toward fully converting research grants to a fund-based system promptly, reduce researchers’ burdensome administrative work, and secure research time.",""],[1,"38","2","Advanced Research Facilities Development and Sharing","Promote the development, shared use, and upgrading of 158 advanced research facilities and equipment.",""],[1,"38","2","AI for Science Programme","Promote “AI for Science,” which applies AI to scientific research to accelerate new discoveries and understanding.",""],[1,"38","3","University Hospital Education, Research, and Facilities Support","While clarifying how to balance the education, research, and medical care functions of university hospitals, support will be provided to strengthen educational and research functions and management capacity, improve working conditions, and urgently improve aging facilities and equipment.",""],[1,"38","4","Girls’ STEM Career Pathway Support Initiative","Promote integrated industry-academia-government and community initiatives to provide girls in middle and high school with continuous opportunities to learn cutting-edge science and technology and pursue science and engineering careers.",""],[1,"38","4","Support Programme for Young Female Researchers","Promote support for young female researchers so that they can continue their research regardless of life events.",""]],"19":[[1,"11","1","Government-Supported Startup Finance Mechanism","Develop startup finance by further strengthening the supply of funds from government-affiliated financial institutions and others as a catalyst for private funds.",""],[1,"11","1","Public Procurement Demand Creation Policy","Work on creating and expanding new demand through procurement by government agencies, including defense procurement.",""],[1,"11","1","Regulatory and Standards-Based Market Creation","Work on creating and expanding new demand through the introduction of regulations and standards.",""],[1,"13","3","Growth Investment-Promoting Financial Strategy","A “Financial Strategy to Promote Growth Investment” will be formulated.",""],[1,"13","3","Financial Institution Funding and Growth Support Strengthening","The functions of financial institutions in providing funds and supporting growth will be strengthened.",""],[1,"13","3","Deep and Broad Financial Market Development","A deep and broad financial market will be realized.",""],[1,"13","3","Regional Financial Capacity Strengthening","Regional financial capacity will be strengthened.",""],[1,"13","3","Asset Owner Function Enhancement","The functions of asset owners will be improved.",""],[1,"13","3","Household Stable Asset Formation Promotion","Stable asset formation by households will be promoted.",""],[1,"13","3","On-Chain Finance Promotion","On-chain finance will be promoted.",""],[1,"13","3","Individual Government Bond Investor Expansion","The domestic investor base will be expanded by making government bonds for individuals more attractive.",""]],"20":[[1,"21","4","Rules-Based Free Trade Regime Expansion","Work to maintain and expand the rules-based free trade system.",""],[1,"21","4","CPTPP Expansion and Institutional Strengthening","While advancing domestic measures for the CPTPP, promote the expansion of signatories and amendment of the agreement, strengthen cooperation with like-minded partners outside the agreement, and strengthen the system and its functions.",""],[1,"21","4","Overseas Business Expansion Support","Promote support for companies' overseas expansion, including infrastructure systems, in regions including the Global South.",""],[1,"21","4","Japan-US Strategic Investment Initiative Implementation","To steadily implement the Japan-US Strategic Investment Initiative as part of the agreement between Japan and the United States, take necessary measures for the Japan Bank for International Cooperation and Nippon Export and Investment Insurance.",""],[1,"21","6","EPA Promotion and WTO Reform","Including the promotion of EPAs and WTO reform.",""]],"22":[[1,"26","6","Comprehensive Foreign Resident Policy and Orderly Coexistence Measures","Based on the Comprehensive Measures for the Acceptance of Foreign Nationals and Orderly Coexistence, the government will respond resolutely to problematic conduct, including illegal acts and deviations from rules by some foreign nationals, and further advance initiatives to address public anxiety and feelings of unfairness.",""],[1,"26","6","Residence Permit Fee Revision","The government will review residence permit fees.",""],[1,"26","6","JESTA Electronic Travel Authorization Introduction","The government will introduce the electronic travel authorization system, JESTA.",""]],"24":[[1,"17","3","Strategic Inbound Tourism Attraction Programme","Pursue strategic attraction of inbound visitors, including promotion of travel to regional areas.",""],[1,"17","3","Domestic Exchange and Outbound Travel Expansion","Expand domestic exchange and outbound travel.",""],[1,"17","3","Tourism Industry Resilience Strengthening Programme","Strengthen the resilience of tourism industries such as the accommodation industry.",""],[1,"17","3","Overtourism Management Measures","Strengthen measures against overtourism while ensuring the quality of residents' lives.",""]],"26":[[1,"20","4","Dormant Deposits-Based NPO Support Programme","Work to support NPO corporations through the system for utilizing dormant deposits and other means.",""],[1,"20","4","Public Interest Activity Promotion Initiative","Work to promote public interest activities by public interest corporations and trusts.",""],[1,"20","4","Pay-for-Success Financing Dissemination Initiative","Work to disseminate PFS.",""],[1,"20","7","Outcome-Based Private Contracting Mechanism","Outcome-based private outsourcing contract method.",""]],"27":[[1,"19","6","Gender Pay Gap and Workplace Employment Management Reform","Addressing workplace employment management issues, including correcting gender-based wage disparities",""],[1,"19","6","Women’s Participation in Growth Strategy Fields","Promoting women’s participation in fields covered by the growth strategy",""],[1,"19","6","Work and Family Care Reconciliation Support","Supporting the reconciliation of work with childcare and caregiving",""],[1,"19","6","Gender-Specific Health Issue Response","Addressing health issues based on sex differences",""],[1,"20","1","Gender Role Attitudes Elimination Initiative","Strongly advance efforts based on 66 relevant basic plans, etc., to eliminate fixed gender-based division-of-roles attitudes and related barriers.",""]],"28":[[1,"26","1","New Technology Crime and CBRNE Terrorism Countermeasures","Deterrence of and responses to crimes that abuse new technologies and CBRNE terrorism",""],[1,"26","1","Comprehensive Anti-Fraud Measures 2.0","Promotion of the Comprehensive Measures 2.0 to Protect the Public from Fraud toward the eradication of Tokuryu",""],[1,"26","1","Stalker Countermeasures","Strengthening stalker countermeasures",""],[1,"26","1","Illicit Drug Countermeasures","Strengthening illicit drug countermeasures",""],[1,"26","1","Gold Smuggling and Cash Courier Countermeasures","Strengthening gold smuggling and cash courier countermeasures",""],[1,"26","1","Law Enforcement and Drug Control Capacity Development","Developing the systems of the police, customs, Regional Bureaus of Health and Welfare Narcotics Control Departments, and prosecutors","Police | Customs | Regional Bureaus of Health and Welfare Narcotics Control Departments | Prosecutors"],[1,"26","1","Security Camera Expansion","Strengthening efforts to encourage the expansion of security cameras",""],[1,"26","1","Beneficial Ownership Information Registration Legislation","Promoting legislation without delay for the registration of information on the beneficial owners of corporations",""],[1,"26","2","Recidivism Prevention and Probation Officer Support","Work on preventing recidivism, including support for probation officers.",""],[1,"26","2","Enhanced Access to Justice","Work on enhancing access to justice.",""],[1,"26","2","Judicial Digital Transformation","Work on judicial digital transformation.",""],[1,"26","2","Judicial Diplomacy","Work on judicial diplomacy.",""],[1,"26","2","Appropriate Operation of the Retrial System","Work on the appropriate operation of the retrial system based on past reflections.",""],[1,"26","2","Crime Victim Support","Work on support for crime victims and others affected.",""],[1,"26","2","Traffic Safety Measures","Work on traffic safety measures.",""],[1,"26","7","Police, Fire and Self-Defense Equipment Enhancement","Enhancement of equipment and materials for the police, fire services and Self-Defense Forces.",""],[1,"26","7","Rehabilitation Facility Support","Enhancement of support for rehabilitation facilities.",""],[1,"26","7","Employment Support for Former Offenders","Strengthening employment support for persons who have committed crimes and others.",""],[1,"26","7","Local Government Coordination for Offender Reintegration","Strengthening collaboration with local governments.",""],[1,"26","7","Comprehensive Legal Aid Enhancement","Enhancement of comprehensive legal assistance.",""],[1,"26","7","Regional Justice Personnel and Facility Development","Development of regional justice personnel and facilities.",""],[1,"26","7","Support for Young and Mid-Career Lawyers","Necessary support to expand the fields of activity for young and mid-career legal professionals undertaking public-interest activities.",""],[1,"26","7","Legal System Development Assistance","Assistance for legal system development.",""]],"29":[[1,"26","3","Measures Against Malicious Business Practices","Advance responses adapted to social changes, including measures against malicious business practices",""],[1,"26","3","Food Safety Assurance Measures","Advance responses adapted to social changes, including ensuring food safety",""],[1,"26","3","Digital Transaction Consumer Protection Measures","Advance responses adapted to social changes, including the expansion of digital transactions",""],[1,"26","3","Local Consumer Administration Strengthening","Continuously strengthen local consumer administration",""],[1,"26","3","Food Loss Reduction Initiative","Promote food loss reduction",""],[1,"26","3","Consumer Education Promotion","Promote consumer education",""]],"30":[[1,"18","5","Cultural Property Preservation and Enhancement Programme","Preservation, repair and enhancement of the value of cultural properties for regional revitalization using cultural resources and transmission to the next generation",""],[1,"18","5","Traditional Culture and Performing Arts Promotion","Promotion of traditional events and performing arts, food culture and other living cultures",""],[1,"18","5","Performing Arts Expansion and Theatre Access Initiative","Promotion of the performing arts, including addressing the shortage of theatres in the Tokyo metropolitan area",""],[1,"18","5","Global Expansion of Ballet and Performing Arts","Global expansion of ballet and other performing arts, beginning with the New National Theatre",""],[1,"18","5","Museum and Theatre Function Enhancement Programme","Strengthening the functions of museums, theatres and other facilities",""],[1,"18","5","Dialect Preservation and Transmission Initiative","Preservation and transmission of dialects",""],[1,"18","5","Bookstore Revitalization Initiative","Revitalization of bookstores",""],[1,"18","5","Cultural Content Digital Archiving Programme","Advancing digital archiving so that manga, live-action works including films, and music including records from the Meiji, Taisho and Showa periods, which are the sources of current content, are not lost or dispersed and remain for future generations",""],[1,"18","5","Inclusive Cultural Participation Programme","Enhancing opportunities for children and persons with disabilities to view and experience cultural works",""],[1,"18","6","Media Arts National Center Hub Development","Develop a hub through public-private partnership with the functions of the Media Arts National Center (provisional name).",""],[1,"18","6","National Theatre Redevelopment","Redevelop the National Theatre under the responsibility of the national government toward its reopening in fiscal year 2033.",""],[1,"18","6","National Archives New Building Development","Work toward the opening of the new building of the National Archives.",""],[1,"18","7","Creator and Related Human Resources Development Programme","Promote the development of creators through the process of creation and dissemination, as well as the development of related human resources.",""],[1,"18","7","Comprehensive Anti-Piracy Measures","Fundamentally strengthen measures against piracy.",""],[1,"18","10","Cultural Properties Takumi Project Continuation","Steady continuation of the “Cultural Properties Takumi Project”.",""],[1,"18","10","National Cultural Property Restoration Center Development","Development of the National Center for Cultural Property Restoration and Conservation and establishment of its staffing structure.",""],[1,"18","10","Takamatsuzuka Mural Conservation Facility Development","Promotion of the development of the Takamatsuzuka Tumulus Mural Conservation, Management and Public Utilization Facility (provisional name).",""],[1,"18","10","Japan Heritage Revitalization Initiative","Revitalization of Japan Heritage.",""],[1,"18","10","Japan Expo Promotion Programme","Promotion of the “Japan Expo”.",""],[1,"18","10","Japanese Film and Art Promotion","Promotion of Japanese films, including international co-productions, and art.",""],[1,"18","10","Cultural Materials Digital Archiving Initiative","For example, the National Diet Library is conducting digital archiving of publications and SP records, while the National Film Archive is conducting digital archiving of films.",""]],"31":[[1,"18","8","Corporate Employee Health Promotion Support Programme","Support companies working to maintain employee health",""],[1,"18","8","Accessible Community Exercise Space Provision","Secure accessible places for everyday exercise",""],[1,"18","9","Sports Digital Transformation and Tourism Promotion","To promote the transformation of sports into a growth industry and the promotion of martial arts and sports tourism, promote digital transformation, including the use of sports complexes and esports.",""],[1,"18","9","Major International Sports Event Support","Provide various forms of support for attracting and hosting major international sporting events.",""],[1,"18","9","International Sports Competitiveness Development","Work to improve international competitive ability.",""],[1,"18","9","Sports Integrity Assurance Initiative","Work to ensure integrity.",""],[1,"18","9","Sports Viewing Access Expansion","Work to secure opportunities to view sports.",""],[1,"18","9","Parasports Promotion Programme","Promote parasports.",""],[1,"18","9","International Sports Exchange Programme","Work on international exchange.",""]],"32":[[1,"21","5","Official Development Assistance Expansion","Expand ODA in various forms, including the utilization of JICA Overseas Cooperation Volunteers, responses to humanitarian crises and reconstruction needs, and cooperation with international financial institutions to address global challenges.",""],[1,"21","3","Responsible Japanese Diplomacy and Diplomatic Capability Strengthening","Develop “Responsible Japanese Diplomacy” to lead a world experiencing increasing division and confrontation toward openness and cooperation, and fundamentally strengthen diplomatic power.",""],[1,"21","3","International Partnership and Alliance Cooperation Strengthening","Strengthen cooperation with like-minded countries and institutions, including the United States-Japan alliance, the G7, ASEAN, Australia, India, the Republic of Korea, the European Union, and NATO, as well as with the Global South.",""],[1,"21","3","Free and Open Indo-Pacific Promotion","Promote initiatives for an evolved “Free and Open Indo-Pacific (FOIP)”.",""],[1,"21","3","Security Assistance and Security-Oriented ODA Expansion","Expand the scale of Official Security Assistance (OSA) and Official Development Assistance (ODA) contributing to security and economic security, thereby contributing to regional peace and stability.",""],[1,"21","5","Ukraine Support Programme","Continue support for Ukraine.",""],[1,"21","5","Nuclear Disarmament Initiative","Promote efforts toward a world without nuclear weapons.",""],[1,"21","5","United Nations Function Strengthening Reform","Strengthen United Nations functions, including reform of the Security Council and increasing the number of Japanese officials.",""],[1,"21","5","Cultural Diplomacy Enhancement","Enhance cultural diplomacy.",""],[1,"21","5","Peace Mediation Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen peace mediation functions.",""],[1,"21","5","North Korea Issues Resolution and Normalization","Comprehensively resolve issues including abductions, nuclear weapons, and missiles based on the Japan-DPRK Pyongyang Declaration, settle the unfortunate past, and achieve normalization of diplomatic relations.",""],[1,"21","5","Diplomatic and Consular Capacity Strengthening","Fundamentally strengthen the diplomatic and consular implementation system by strengthening personnel and making overseas missions more resilient while pursuing rationalization and efficiency.",""]],"33":[[1,"20","5","Diplomatic Power Strengthening","Japan will first strengthen its diplomatic power.",""],[1,"20","5","National Defense Capability Strengthening","Japan will proactively strengthen its defense capabilities.",""],[1,"20","5","Integrated National Power Coordination","Japan will organically link its diplomatic power, defense power, economic power, technological power, information power, and human resources power, thereby strengthening its comprehensive national power.",""],[1,"21","1","Defense Transformation Review and Implementation","Accelerate consideration of the three documents and realize the transformation of defense capabilities within five years.",""],[1,"21","1","Defense Buildup Plan Development","Create a Defense Buildup Plan by accumulating the expenses indispensable for protecting Japan's independence and peace.",""],[1,"21","1","Defense Buildup Financing Mechanism","Secure the financial resources for its implementation.",""],[1,"21","1","Public Explanation of Defense Policy and Financing","Explain the matter carefully to the people.",""],[1,"21","1","Maritime Security Capability Enhancement","Strengthen maritime security capabilities.",""],[1,"21","1","Defense and Security Research and Development","Promote research and development.",""],[1,"21","1","Public Infrastructure Development","Develop public infrastructure.",""],[1,"21","1","National Cybersecurity Strengthening","Strengthen cybersecurity.",""],[1,"21","1","International Deterrence Cooperation","Promote international cooperation to improve the deterrence capabilities of Japan and like-minded countries.",""],[1,"21","1","Strategic Energy and Food Foundation Strengthening","Strategically strengthen the foundations supporting people's livelihoods, including energy and food.",""],[1,"21","1","Cross-Government Security Initiatives","Clarify government-wide initiatives.",""],[1,"21","1","Economic, Financial and Fiscal Foundation Strengthening","Continually strengthen the foundations of the economy, finance and public finances, which are the foundation of security.",""],[1,"22","1","Defense Capability Transformation Programme","Transform defense capabilities in both equipment and organizational structures within five years to exercise highly autonomous and resilient capabilities.",""],[1,"22","1","New Warfare Adaptation and Stand-Off Defense Programme","Adapt to 'new ways of warfare' through the use of data and AI, the introduction of unmanned assets, and the strengthening of stand-off defense capabilities that could also be used for counterstrike capabilities.",""],[1,"22","1","Self-Defense Personnel Compensation and Utilization Reform","Promote improvements in the treatment and long-term utilization of Self-Defense personnel, beginning with revision of the salary system.",""],[1,"22","1","Retired Self-Defense Personnel and Family Support Programme","Strengthen initiatives to support retired Self-Defense personnel and their families, including consideration of establishing a new agency.",""],[1,"22","1","Ministry of Defense Organizational Strengthening Reform","Fundamentally strengthen the organization of the Ministry of Defense.","Ministry of Defense"]],"34":[[1,"21","6","Strategic Ministerial Council for Energy and Food Security","Ministerial Council for the Strategic Strengthening of Foundations Supporting the Lives of the People, such as Energy and Food.",""],[1,"21","6","Economic Security Crisis and Growth Investment Review","The handling of crisis-management investments and growth investments in fields of particular importance for economic security will continue to be considered.",""],[1,"23","5","Economic Security Risk Review and Vulnerability Remediation","Conduct a comprehensive overall risk review of the social infrastructure foundations necessary to maintain citizens' livelihoods and industrial activities, including essential goods and logistics such as maritime transport, and take measures to eliminate the vulnerabilities revealed.",""],[1,"23","5","Critical Supply Chain and Manufacturing Base Strengthening","Expand the scope of support to include important foundational goods, including general-purpose goods, the component materials supporting goods whose importance is expected to increase further, and resource circulation, while advancing comprehensive efforts to strengthen supply chains and the manufacturing base from upstream to downstream.",""],[1,"23","5","Government Support for Stable Supply in Market Gaps","Consider further measures for government support in areas where securing a stable supply would be difficult if left to economic rationality.",""],[1,"23","6","Critical Goods Stable Supply Support","Work to ensure the stable supply of critical goods, including support for services indispensable to the supply of critical goods, based on the amended Economic Security Promotion Act and the Japan Bank for International Cooperation Act.",""],[1,"23","6","Economic Security Overseas Business Support","Work to support overseas businesses important from the perspective of economic security (OESA).",""],[1,"23","6","Japan Bank for International Cooperation Institutional Strengthening","Work to strengthen the system, including securing the financial foundation and specialized personnel of the Japan Bank for International Cooperation.",""],[1,"23","6","Comprehensive Economic Security Think Tank Function","Promote securing human resources and improving the environment, aiming to establish a comprehensive economic security think tank function during fiscal year 2026.",""],[1,"23","6","Economic Security Important Technology Nurturing Programme Strengthening","Advance institutional design toward strengthening the Economic Security Important Technology Nurturing Programme in order to promote research and development of specifically designated critical technologies.",""],[1,"23","6","International Joint Research Promotion","Promote international joint research.",""],[1,"23","8","Economic Security Risk Response Strengthening","To strengthen responses to economic security risks such as the leakage of sensitive technologies, the Committee on Foreign Investment in Japan",""]],"35":[[1,"24","7","Volcanic Disaster Countermeasures","Undertake measures against volcanic disasters such as Mount Fuji eruptions.",""],[1,"24","2","National Land Resilience Measures","To protect the lives and property of the people today and in the future from crises such as increasingly severe and frequent natural disasters and aging infrastructure, and to underpin a strong economy, the government will decisively implement Reiwa-era national land resilience measures.",""],[1,"24","4","National Resilience Measures Strengthening Initiative","Promote measures based on the National Resilience Annual Plan 2026 by utilizing the \"Strong and Prosperous Japan\" Investment Framework, and strengthen both hardware and software measures through the full use of technology.",""],[1,"24","5","Disaster Management Agency and Whole-of-Government Command Reform","Establish the Disaster Management Agency and strengthen whole-of-government command-and-control functions consistently from before a disaster occurs through recovery and reconstruction.",""],[1,"24","5","Regional Disaster Management Bureau Support","Through the regional disaster management bureaus established alongside it, support the improvement of regional disaster preparedness capacity.",""],[1,"24","5","Simulation-Based Disaster Risk Assessment and Preparedness","Utilize disaster risk assessments through simulations to strengthen the disaster preparedness capacity of companies and communities.",""],[1,"24","6","Disaster Management Workforce Recruitment and Training","Consideration of securing and training human resources in the disaster management field, including improving the treatment of emergency mobilization personnel to ensure a rapid initial response.",""],[1,"24","6","National Disaster Support System Strengthening","Proceed with enhancing and strengthening the disaster support system and functions of the national government, including regional branch offices and other bodies, beginning with the development of crisis management housing.",""],[1,"24","6","Ship-Based Medical Care Delivery System","Promote the development of a system for providing ship-based medical care.",""],[1,"24","6","Disaster Waste Management System Enhancement","Enhance the disaster waste management system.",""],[1,"24","7","Major Earthquake Disaster Countermeasures","Promote measures against the Kuril Trench earthquake, Japan Trench earthquake, Tokyo metropolitan earthquake, and Nankai Trough earthquake.",""],[1,"24","7","Volcanic Disaster Research Programme","Undertake survey and research through the Volcano Research and Investigation Promotion Headquarters.",""],[1,"24","7","Volcanic Disaster Human Resources Development","Undertake securing and developing human resources.",""],[1,"24","8","Satellite and AI-Based Firefighting and Disaster Prevention Digital Transformation","Promote firefighting and disaster prevention digital transformation using satellite and AI technologies.",""],[1,"24","8","Advanced Disaster Prevention Meteorological Information System","Advance the sophistication of disaster prevention meteorological information.",""],[1,"24","8","Firefighting and Disaster Prevention Capacity Strengthening","Advance the enhancement and strengthening of firefighting and disaster prevention capabilities, beginning with wildfire response.",""],[1,"24","8","Disaster Prevention Research and Industry Development Initiative","Using crisis management investment and growth investment, promote research and development in disaster prevention technologies and nurture the disaster prevention industry and its overseas expansion.",""],[1,"24","9","Disaster Victim Support System Strengthening","Strengthen the support system for disaster victims.",""],[1,"24","9","Evacuation Living Environment Improvement","Fundamentally improve the living environment during evacuation.",""],[1,"24","9","Public-Private Disaster Response Workforce Mechanism","Advance the securing of personnel through public-private collaboration.",""],[1,"24","9","Disaster Supplies and Equipment Management System","Advance the development of supplies and equipment and the establishment of an operational system.",""],[1,"24","9","Disaster Victim Mental Health Care","Work on mental health care for disaster victims.",""],[1,"24","9","Disaster-Resilient Shelter and Emergency Functionality Enhancement","Strengthen the disaster resilience of evacuation shelters and other facilities and work to ensure their functionality in emergencies.",""],[1,"24","10","High-Standard Road Missing-Link Elimination","Elimination of missing links on high-standard roads",""],[1,"24","10","Utility Pole Removal Programme","Utility pole removal",""],[1,"24","10","Heavy Snowfall Countermeasure Programme","Heavy snowfall measures",""],[1,"25","1","Disaster Lessons Transmission for Behavioral Change","Behavioral change through transmitting disaster lessons is important for disaster prevention and mitigation.",""],[1,"25","1","Phase-Free Disaster Prevention Initiative","Phase-free initiatives are important for disaster prevention and mitigation.",""],[1,"25","1","Disaster Prevention Education Programme","Promote disaster prevention education.",""],[1,"25","1","Practical Disaster Awareness Initiative","Promote practical dissemination and awareness-raising.",""],[1,"25","2","Government Alternative Bases and Capital Disaster Resilience Enhancement","Advance the development of arrangements to strengthen disaster-prevention performance at government alternative bases and in the capital core.",""],[1,"25","2","Public-Private Disaster Resilience Financing Mechanism","Maximize the use of private funds and private-sector vitality through public-private partnerships and regulatory relaxation.",""],[1,"25","3","Alternative Capital Functions Region and Deputy Capital Development","From the perspective of ensuring the continuity of national social functions and forming a polycentric, decentralized economic zone, initiatives will be advanced to develop an alternative region for central capital functions and a deputy capital, on the assumption that Bill 94 will be enacted.",""]],"36":[[1,"25","5","Disaster Infrastructure Restoration and Development","Promote the restoration and development of infrastructure.",""],[1,"25","5","Disaster Public Housing Development","Promote the development of disaster public housing.",""],[1,"25","5","Post-Disaster Community Reconstruction Planning","Promote reconstruction-oriented community development.",""],[1,"25","5","Livelihood and Livelihood-Business Reconstruction Support","Promote the reconstruction of the lives and livelihoods of disaster victims.",""],[1,"25","5","Local and Traditional Industry Revival Programme","Promote the revival and development of local industries and traditional industries.",""],[1,"25","5","Accelerated Cadastral Survey and Legal Affairs Mapping","Promote the acceleration of cadastral surveys and the creation of Legal Affairs Bureau maps.","Legal Affairs Bureau"],[1,"25","6","National and Social Functions Continuity and Secondary Capital Development Bill","Bill on promoting measures to secure the continuity of national and social functions and measures related to the development of a secondary capital.",""],[1,"25","6","Basic Policy for Great East Japan Earthquake Reconstruction","Basic Policy for Reconstruction from the Great East Japan Earthquake in and after the 'Second Reconstruction and Revitalization Period' (Cabinet decision on June 20, 2025).",""]],"37":[[1,"25","4","Government-Led Reconstruction of Nuclear Disaster-Affected Areas","The government will take the lead in promoting the reconstruction and regeneration of areas affected by the nuclear disaster.",""],[1,"25","4","AI and Robotics Development for Nuclear Accident Response","Development and demonstration of AI and robotic technologies will also be carried out toward bringing the nuclear accident under control.",""],[1,"25","4","Safe and Steady Nuclear Plant Decommissioning","Decommissioning will be advanced safely and steadily.",""],[1,"25","4","Removal of Import Restrictions on Fukushima Products","Efforts will be made to eliminate import restrictions.",""],[1,"25","4","Fisheries Industry Support Programme","Efforts will be made to support the fisheries industry.",""],[1,"25","4","Rumor and Misinformation Countermeasures","Efforts will be made to address reputational damage and false information.",""],[1,"25","4","Promotion of Recycled Reconstruction Soil Use","The use of recycled reconstruction soil will be promoted through fostering public understanding.",""],[1,"25","4","Pathway for Off-Site Final Disposal","A concrete pathway toward final disposal outside the prefecture from 2030 onward will be developed.",""],[1,"25","4","Decontamination and Infrastructure Development in Designated Return Areas","Decontamination and infrastructure development will be carried out in designated return residential areas for residents’ return and migration.",""],[1,"25","4","Forest Management in Difficult-to-Return Areas","The resumption of forest management within difficult-to-return areas will be advanced.",""],[1,"25","4","Review of Activity Liberalization in Difficult-to-Return Areas","Consideration will be advanced regarding the liberalization of activities within difficult-to-return areas.",""],[1,"25","4","Agricultural and Livelihood Reconstruction Programme","Efforts will be made to rebuild lives and livelihoods, including through the resumption of farming.",""],[1,"25","4","Fukushima Innovation and Research-Driven Industrial Development","The initiatives of the Fukushima Innovation Coast Initiative and the Fukushima Institute for Research, Education and Innovation will be advanced in coordination with the Regional Future Strategy and other measures to promote industrial development.",""],[1,"25","4","Mental Health Care for Earthquake and Tsunami-Affected Areas","The government will respond to challenges such as mental health care in earthquake- and tsunami-affected areas by using measures across the government.",""]],"38":[[1,"28","5","Long-Term Economic and Fiscal Plan","The plan renews the Economic and Fiscal Revitalization Plan and establishes this chapter as a Long-Term Economic and Fiscal Plan based on responsible proactive fiscal policy.",""],[1,"28","5","Fiscal Management Objectives Framework","Setting fiscal management objectives",""],[1,"29","2","Multi-Year Debt Sustainability Management Framework","Manage over multiple years in a manner consistent with the stable decline of the debt-to-GDP ratio.",""],[1,"29","3","Debt Sustainability Analysis Mechanism","Analyze the contributions of the primary balance, GDP, net interest payments, and fiscal balance to the debt-to-GDP ratio, and work to ensure fiscal sustainability.",""],[1,"29","4","Fiscal Expenditure and Revenue Review and Debt Reduction Policy","In future budget formulation, review both expenditures and revenues, scrutinize the fiscal scale that can be maintained while steadily reducing the debt-to-GDP ratio, and give due consideration to securing market confidence.",""],[1,"29","4","Annual Government Bond Issuance Planning","Specify the annual government bond issuance amount.",""],[1,"29","11","Annual Government Bond Issuance Planning","The full-year government bond issuance amount for fiscal year 2027 will be considered during the budget formulation process while monitoring economic and tax revenue trends and paying attention to securing market confidence.",""],[1,"29","11","Medium-Term Debt-Compatible Fiscal Management","The fiscal scale will be managed flexibly in a manner consistent with the medium-term debt path.",""],[1,"31","3","Fiscal Management Transparency and Communication Mechanism","To secure market confidence through strengthened communication, provide the public and domestic and overseas market participants with transparent and consistent explanations of fiscal management, including the above review.",""],[1,"31","4","Multi-Dimensional Economic and Fiscal Monitoring Mechanism","To secure market confidence, economic trends and fiscal indicators are analyzed and verified from multiple angles.",""],[1,"31","5","Economic and Fiscal Scenario Analysis and Review Mechanism","When estimating the future economic and fiscal outlook, utilize the knowledge of external experts, conduct analysis based on a wide range of possibilities in preparation for uncertainties surrounding economic, price, and interest-rate trends and policy effects, and use it to review economic and fiscal management.",""],[1,"39","7","Medium- to Long-Term Economic and Fiscal Projections Monitoring","Position the medium- to long-term economic and fiscal projections as a foundation for clearly presenting the assumptions, policy effects, and risks of responsible proactive fiscal policy, confirm the pathway toward realizing the economic and fiscal vision every six months, analyze progress against previous assumptions, and conduct appropriate macroeconomic and fiscal management.",""]],"40":[[1,"33","1","Sustainable Doctor Helicopter Operations","Ensure the safe and sustainable operation of doctor helicopters.",""],[1,"32","5","Healthcare Productivity and Flexible Staffing Initiative","Promote further efforts toward improving productivity and making staffing more flexible through DX/AX and team-based medical care, including multidisciplinary collaboration.",""],[1,"32","5","Healthcare Management Information Transparency Mechanism","Advance the visualization of management information and understand actual management conditions.",""],[1,"32","5","Healthcare Management Stability and Workforce Treatment Measures","Appropriately respond to changes in prices and wages, while securing management stability and improving staff treatment.",""],[1,"32","6","Medical Fee Adjustment Mechanism","If economic and price trends change substantially from the outlook at the time of the FY2026 medical fee revision and cause difficulties in the management of medical institutions, further necessary adjustments, including additions and deductions to medical fees, will be made during the FY2027 budget formulation process.",""],[1,"32","6","Care and Disability Welfare Fee Revision","In the next revisions of long-term care fees and disability welfare service fees, while appropriately responding to price fluctuations, including the standard reimbursement amounts for assistive devices, efforts will be made to realize treatment improvements comparable to those of other occupations.",""],[1,"32","6","Care Provider Management Database","In the next revisions of long-term care fees and disability welfare service fees, efforts will be made to develop and use a management database.",""],[1,"32","6","Sustainable Welfare Service System Review","The appropriate fee and system arrangements will be examined to ensure the quality and improvement of services and the sustainability of the system, including responses to the rapid increase in the costs of disability welfare services.",""],[1,"32","6","Essential Worker and Service Provision Reform","Institutional reform will be promptly initiated to maintain nationwide service provision systems, including securing the necessary essential workers in fields such as medical care, long-term care, childcare, and welfare.",""],[1,"32","7","Hospital Bed Capacity Optimization","Toward 2040, steadily implement the appropriate optimization of the number of hospital beds.",""],[1,"32","8","Medical Benefit Expenditure and Fee Reform","Reforms will continue, including fundamentally reviewing the next revision of the Medical Care Expenditure Optimization Plan while basically reflecting economic and price trends in medical fees.",""],[1,"33","1","Medical Institution Coordination and Community Care Integration","Promote the coordination, reorganization and consolidation of medical institutions, deepen integrated community care systems, and construct high-quality, efficient medical and long-term care service delivery systems suited to local circumstances.",""],[1,"33","1","Emergency Medical Care System","Ensure the emergency medical care system.",""],[1,"33","1","Patient-Centered End-of-Life Care","Provide appropriate patient-centered medical care and support at the final stage of life, including end-of-life care.",""],[1,"33","1","Community-Based Mental Healthcare Planning","Promote initiatives concerning mental healthcare based on community medical care visions.",""],[1,"33","1","Home Nursing Service Provision","Promote the appropriate implementation of home nursing.",""],[1,"33","1","Flexible Care and Disability Welfare Services","Promote the provision of flexible long-term care and disability welfare services in mountainous and depopulated areas.",""]],"42":[[1,"35","1","Aggressive Preventive Healthcare Promotion","Promote “aggressive preventive healthcare,” with relevant institutions working together on health promotion, disease prevention including obesity, early detection, early intervention, and behavioral change.",""],[1,"35","1","Health Literacy Improvement Programme","Improve health literacy, including nutrition and dietary habits.",""],[1,"35","1","Community Pharmacy and Pharmacist Strengthening","Strengthen pharmacy functions and the role played by pharmacists in contributing to the health promotion of local residents.",""],[1,"35","1","School-Age Health Examination Review","Review how health examinations for school-age children should be conducted.",""],[1,"35","1","Vaccination Programme","Promote vaccination.",""],[1,"35","1","Infectious Disease Prevention and Surveillance Measures","Implement infectious disease measures, including prevention of HIV and sexually transmitted infections and wastewater surveillance.",""],[1,"35","1","Cancer Screening and Follow-Up Uptake Improvement","Improve participation rates for cancer screenings and detailed examinations.",""],[1,"35","1","Lifestyle Disease Prevention Programme","Promote the prevention of lifestyle-related diseases, including cardiovascular disease and diabetes.",""],[1,"35","1","Universal Dental Checkup Expansion","Give concrete form to the so-called universal dental checkup system, including expanding the scope of periodontal disease examinations and further enhancing dental checkups for the working-age population.",""],[1,"35","1","Dental Disease Prevention and Oral Health Management","Implement dental disease measures and oral health management based on the relationship between oral and overall health.",""],[1,"35","1","Dementia Early Diagnosis and Response Programme","Promote early diagnosis and early response for dementia.",""],[1,"35","1","Integrated Rehabilitation Continuity Programme","Promote seamless rehabilitation through prevention, medical care, and long-term care.",""],[1,"35","2","Comprehensive Disease Countermeasures Programme","Promote disease countermeasures for cancer, stroke, heart disease and other cardiovascular diseases, chronic kidney disease, chronic obstructive pulmonary disease, chronic pain, intractable diseases, allergies, addictions, hearing loss, sleep disorders, and other diseases.",""],[1,"35","2","Transplant Medicine Promotion Measures","Promote transplant medicine measures.",""]],"44":[[1,"35","4","Integrated Child and Family Support Strategy","Based on the Children's Future Strategy and other policies, measures for addressing the declining birthrate and supporting children, young people, and child-rearing are to be promoted powerfully in an integrated and comprehensive manner.",""],[1,"35","4","Integrated Consultation Support at Child and Family Centers","Provide a unified response to consultation support at Child and Family Centers.",""],[1,"35","4","Seamless Pregnancy-to-Parenting Support","Advance seamless support from pregnancy through child-rearing, including maternal and child health policies such as postpartum care.",""],[1,"35","4","Infertility Support Programme","Advance support for infertility and related conditions.",""],[1,"35","4","Childcare Fee Reduction Measure","Advance measures including reducing the burden of childcare fees.",""],[1,"35","4","Early Childhood Education and Childcare Support","Consider and advance support for early childhood education and childcare while taking into account challenges in securing human resources and financial resources.",""],[1,"35","4","Early Childhood Education and Childcare Workforce Improvement","Improve the treatment of childcare workers, kindergarten teachers, and others.",""],[1,"35","4","Official Price Review for Early Childhood Services","Review official prices, including regional classifications, for early childhood education and childcare.",""],[1,"35","5","Children-Centered Action Plan Implementation","The various measures included in the Children-Centered Action Plan 2026 will be promoted.",""],[1,"36","1","Babysitter and Household Support Service Promotion","Promote the use of high-quality babysitting and household support services to help people balance work and family life.",""],[1,"36","1","After-School and Sick-Childcare Enhancement","Enhance after-school places and sick-childcare services, drawing on the vitality of companies and other organizations.",""],[1,"36","1","Housing Supply for Child-Rearing Households","Promote the provision of housing for households raising children.",""],[1,"36","1","Companies Growing Together with Children Initiative","Promote the “Companies Growing Together with Children Initiative” to create a virtuous cycle of corporate support and growth.",""]],"45":[[1,"36","2","Child and Youth Suicide Prevention Council Establishment","Promote the establishment of councils in cooperation with local governments.",""],[1,"36","2","ICT and AI Utilization Review for Child Protection","Examine how ICT and AI should be utilized.",""],[1,"36","2","Child and Youth Suicide Prevention Support System Strengthening","Lead a fundamental strengthening of support systems and raise efforts to address child and youth suicide to a higher level.",""],[1,"36","2","Child Protection Measures Against Sexual Violence","Steadily implement measures to protect children from sexual violence.",""],[1,"36","2","Youth Internet Environment Act Reform","Relevant ministries will cooperate and aim to submit a bill to amend the Youth Internet Environment Act at the next ordinary session of the Diet.",""],[1,"36","4","Early Identification of Children Needing Support","Enable early identification of information on children and others potentially needing support.",""],[1,"36","4","Safe Spaces for Children","Promote the creation of places where children can belong.",""],[1,"36","4","Vulnerable Family and Child Support Programme","Provide support for children in poor households, single-parent families and families before and after divorce, young carers, and pregnant women in difficult circumstances.",""],[1,"36","4","Child Abuse Prevention Measures","Promote child abuse prevention measures.",""],[1,"36","4","Child Guidance Center Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen the systems of child guidance centers.",""],[1,"36","4","Foster Care and Special Adoption Support","Promote social care, including foster placement and special adoption.",""],[1,"36","4","Support and Inclusion for Children with Disabilities","Promote support for children with disabilities, including children with developmental disabilities and children requiring medical care, and inclusion.",""],[1,"36","4","Support for Children from Diverse Backgrounds","Promote initiatives for children from diverse backgrounds.",""],[1,"36","4","Child Death Review System","Promote reviews of child deaths.",""],[1,"36","9","Suicide Prevention Legal Framework Reform","Made statutory by the Partial Amendment Act of the Basic Act for Suicide Prevention.",""],[1,"36","9","Early Review of the Emergency Child Suicide Prevention Plan","Including the early review of the Emergency Strengthening Plan for Children's Suicide Prevention.",""],[1,"36","9","Safe Internet Use Environment for Young People","The Act on the Development of an Environment in Which Young People Can Use the Internet Safely and Securely.",""],[1,"36","9","Joint Parenting and Child Support Compliance Support","Including support for promoting the preparation of joint parenting plans and securing the implementation of child support and parent-child contact.",""]],"46":[[1,"36","3","Basic Design of Youth Policy","Design the basic framework for youth policy based on a large-scale survey.",""],[1,"36","3","Regional Comprehensive Youth Model Projects","Create comprehensive model projects in regions.",""],[1,"36","3","Rich Experience Opportunities for All Children","Enhance opportunities for all children to have rich experiences.",""],[1,"36","3","Youth Participation in Policy Implementation","Promote policy implementation with youth participation, including their appointment as council members.",""]],"49":[[1,"11","7","Research University Systems Coordination Framework","The government will also consider systematizing the three systems, including the Internationally Excellent Research University System and the Promotion Project for Strengthening Regional Core and Distinctive Research Universities, with appropriate division of roles and coordination among the systems.",""]],"50":[[1,"16","7","Regional Living Sphere and Wide-Area Region Formation","Form regional living spheres and new wide-area regions, also utilizing dual-region residence.",""],[1,"16","7","Reiwa Urban Renovation Initiative","Strengthen the earning capacity and disaster prevention capacity of cities through Reiwa urban renovation.",""],[1,"16","7","Wide-Area Urban Collaboration","Promote wide-area collaboration among cities.",""],[1,"16","7","Compact-Plus-Network Development","Deepen and develop the compact-plus-network approach.",""],[1,"16","9","Integrated Vacant Housing and Unknown Land Measures","Promote integrated and comprehensive measures for vacant houses that contribute to disaster prevention and for land with unidentified owners.",""],[1,"16","9","Quality Real Estate Stock and Housing Infrastructure Development","Work on the formation, distribution and utilization of high-quality real estate stock, maximizing the value of housing stock, and rebuilding the foundations that support housing and living.",""],[1,"16","9","Mortgage Interest Rate Risk Awareness Initiative","Take comprehensive measures, including public awareness of mortgage interest rate risks.",""],[1,"16","11","Integrated Redevelopment of Former Base Sites and Naha Airport","A concept by Okinawa's business community and local governments aiming for the integrated use of future former base-return sites and Naha Airport.",""],[1,"16","11","Urban Renaissance Legal Reform","Act Partially Amending the Act on Special Measures concerning Urban Renaissance, etc. (Act No. 23 of 2026).",""],[1,"16","11","Measures for Land with Unknown Owners","Initiatives based on the Basic Policy on Promoting Measures for Land with Unknown Owners, including cadastral surveys, creation of registry office maps, and inheritance registration.",""],[1,"16","11","Real Estate Appraisal Workforce Development","Including securing personnel for the real estate appraisal profession that supports public land valuation.",""]],"52":[[1,"16","8","Comprehensive Infrastructure Management Promotion","Promote comprehensive infrastructure management.",""],[1,"16","8","Preventive Infrastructure Maintenance and Visualization","Shift maintenance to preventive maintenance and promote visualization.",""],[1,"16","8","Integrated Infrastructure Renewal and Urban Reorganization","Coordinate measures to address aging infrastructure with urban development, and promote priority-based measures, consolidation and reorganization, and dispersal through new technologies.",""],[1,"16","8","Cross-Regional Infrastructure Management Collaboration","Promote broad-area and cross-sectoral collaboration and cooperation among entities supporting infrastructure management.",""],[1,"16","8","Building and Urban Digital Transformation Initiative","Advance building and urban digital transformation and Geo AI initiatives toward more sophisticated urban development.",""]],"53":[[1,"39","2","Local Government Administrative and Digital Transformation","Promote local government AX/DX in line with the Priority Plan for the Realization of a Digital Society and other plans.",""],[1,"39","2","Local Government Cybersecurity Strengthening","Strengthen the cybersecurity of local governments.",""],[1,"39","2","Standard-Compliant System Migration and Operational Optimization","Advance migration to standard-compliant systems and optimize their operation.",""],[1,"39","3","Administrative Service Productivity Reform","Advance reforms to increase the productivity of administrative services while taking proposals from local governments into account.",""]],"54":[[1,"28","3","Integrated Policy Package Coordination","Implement various policy packages in close mutual coordination.",""],[1,"39","4","Integrated Fiscal Reform Review Framework","The reform’s progress-management and review function will be reorganized and upgraded into a new framework that integrally reviews expenditure reform, crisis-management and growth investment, policy effects, and fiscal indicators.",""],[1,"39","5","Annual Progress Review of Key Policies","Under this new framework, progress on important medium- to long-term policies underpinning citizens’ lives will be reviewed annually under the Council for Economic and Fiscal Policy.",""],[1,"39","6","Policy Reform Progress Monitoring and Evaluation Mechanism","Each promoting entity continuously checks the implementation status of reforms in accordance with the content of the policies and their stage of progress.",""],[1,"39","6","Tax Incentive Subsidy and Fund Review Reform","Through the review of tax incentives, subsidies, and funds, the cost-effectiveness of policies will be verified from the perspective of whether subsidies and other support generate social value commensurate with expenditure, while expenditure reform is pursued.",""],[1,"39","6","Public-Private Fund Guideline Reform and Profitability Improvement","Efforts will be advanced toward the effective utilization and improvement of returns of public-private funds, including the revision of guidelines.",""],[1,"39","8","Growth Strategy Policy Effect Monitoring and Verification","Also, while taking into account the grasping and verification of the actual micro- and macro-level effects of the \"Growth Strategy\" policies by the Japan Growth Strategy Council, in medium- to long-term economic and fiscal estimates, the relationship among investment, economic growth, and tax revenues...",""],[1,"40","1","Continuous Improvement of Analytical Methods and Models","Promote continuous improvement of analytical methods and models, including more consistent understanding.",""],[1,"40","2","Comprehensive Plan Review Mechanism","The Council on Economic and Fiscal Policy shall, in principle, conduct a comprehensive review of the entire Plan every five years.",""],[1,"40","2","Plan Revision Based on Comprehensive Review","The Plan shall be revised as necessary, taking into account trends in the economy, prices, interest rates and tax revenues, policy effects, and changes in fiscal indicators.",""],[1,"40","4","Integrated Evidence-Based Budget Management","Use EBPM as a tool to advance budget formulation, execution, review, and reflection in budgets for the following fiscal years as an integrated whole.",""],[1,"40","4","Government Policy Analysis Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen the capabilities within government responsible for policy-effect analysis, cost-effectiveness analysis, and data analysis.",""],[1,"40","4","Real-Time Economic Data Utilization","Promote the use of real-time data and high-frequency data to improve the accuracy of understanding the actual state of the economy.",""],[1,"40","4","Evidence-Based Policy Deliberation and Review Mechanism","Clearly present the premises of such analyses and the way policy effects are considered, and use them in discussions, reviews, and verifications at the Council on Economic and Fiscal Policy.",""]],"55":[[1,"4","3","Integrated Social Security and Tax Reform","Promotion of integrated reform of social security and taxation",""],[1,"4","3","Sustainable Social Security System for a Growth-Oriented Economy","Sustainable social security system suited to a growth-oriented economy",""],[1,"6","1","Coordinated Monetary Policy for Price Stability","The Government will continue to work closely with the Bank of Japan and work together to realize sustainable economic growth under price stability without a return to deflation.",""],[1,"6","3","Multidimensional Fiscal and Economic Analysis Strengthening","Strengthen multifaceted analysis using various economic and fiscal indicators, as well as analysis that takes uncertainty into account.",""],[1,"6","3","Growth-Oriented Budget Formulation Reform","A shift to budget formulation appropriate for strengthening economic growth and expanding the nominal size of the economy.",""],[1,"6","3","Strong and Prosperous Japan Investment Framework","The 'Strong and Prosperous Japan' Investment Framework for crisis-management investment and growth investment.",""],[1,"10","3","Strong and Prosperous Japan Investment Framework","Create the “Strong and Prosperous Japan” Investment Framework for crisis-management and growth investment.",""],[1,"6","3","Reduction of Supplementary Budget Dependence","A departure from dependence on supplementary budgets.",""],[1,"6","4","FY2027 Budget Formulation","As the first budget reflecting this fundamental overhaul of budget formulation, the FY2027 budget will be formulated.",""],[1,"6","4","Medium- and Long-Term Economic and Fiscal Plan","Chapter 3 of this Basic Policy will be formulated as a \"Medium- and Long-Term Economic and Fiscal Plan\" based on responsible proactive fiscal policy.",""],[1,"6","5","Whole-Plan Implementation Review Mechanism","Based on reviews of the Regional Future Strategy, all-generation social security, and other sectoral areas, the implementation status of the entire plan shall be reviewed.",""],[1,"5","8","Fiscal Management and Government Practice Reform","Under a new fiscal management policy, the government will correct the harmful effects of single-year fiscalism, review established practices and precedents without hesitation, and formulate, concretize, and decisively implement measures truly necessary to strengthen national capacity and improve people's lives.",""]],"56":[[1,"15","2","Foreign Direct Investment Promotion Programme","Based on the Program for Promoting Foreign Direct Investment in Japan (2026), initiatives will be strengthened, making use of the special zone system and Regional Future Grants.",""],[1,"15","2","Overseas Startup and Venture Capital Investment Attraction","Investment attraction from overseas startups and venture capital firms will be promoted.",""],[1,"15","8","Accelerated Foreign-Language Legal Translation Programme","Accelerate legal foreign-language translations, focusing on laws frequently requested by foreign companies and aiming to publish English translations within one year of promulgation.",""]],"128":[[1,"11","1","Strategic Research and Social Implementation Programme","Promote initiatives that lead the world's academic frontiers, centered on research and development and social implementation in 17 strategic fields.",""],[1,"11","1","Basic and Early-Career Research Support Programme","Support basic research and challenging research by young researchers.",""],[1,"11","1","International Advanced Research Collaboration Programme","Promote advanced research through the dispatch of Japanese researchers overseas and international joint research.",""],[1,"11","1","Advanced Science and Technology Talent Development Programme","Advance the development of science and technology personnel, including highly specialized human resources.",""],[1,"11","1","Industry-Academia Research Hub and Infrastructure Investment","Form hubs for industry-academia co-creation and build the research infrastructure supporting these efforts.",""],[1,"11","1","New Research University System","Establish a new system relating to a group of new research universities.",""],[1,"11","1","Industry-Academia Degree Programme Support","Support degree programs conducted in collaboration between industry and academia.",""],[1,"11","1","National Research and Development Agency Function Strengthening Reform","Strengthen the functions of national research and development agencies.",""],[1,"11","2","Expo Legacy Social Implementation Initiative","In addition, efforts will be made to realize the social implementation of the many new technologies and services exhibited at the Osaka-Kansai Expo so that they become the core of new industries as an “Expo legacy.”",""],[1,"11","3","Startup Research-to-Commercialization Support Programme","Provide seamless support to startups from research and development through commercialization and social implementation.",""],[1,"11","3","Startup Government Procurement Improvement Plan","Formulate an improvement plan for the early achievement of the 3% target for the share of startups in government procurement.",""],[1,"11","3","Enhanced SBIR Public Procurement Programme","Fundamentally strengthen the SBIR system to promote full-scale procurement by the government through anchor-tenancy-type arrangements.",""],[1,"11","3","Strategic Attraction of Overseas Startup Investors","Strategically attract overseas investors, including leading overseas venture capital firms.",""],[1,"11","3","Domestic Mergers and Acquisitions Market Activation","Revitalize the domestic mergers and acquisitions market.",""],[1,"11","3","Global Startup Innovation Ecosystem","Build a global ecosystem in which funds, human resources, and technologies from Japan and abroad circulate positively.",""]],"129":[[1,"12","1","Fifth Basic Plan for Geospatial Information","Formulate the Fifth Basic Plan within fiscal year 2026.",""],[1,"12","1","New Common Geospatial Information Platform Strategy","Formulate and promote a priority strategy for constructing a new common platform, including the use of AI technology.",""]],"130":[[1,"6","7","Accelerated Collaboration Among Local Governments","Collaboration among local governments will be accelerated.",""],[1,"6","7","Regional Human Resource Development","Regional areas will be supported through human resource development.",""]],"133":[[1,"6","6","All-Generation Social Security Reform","Strengthen social security reform to simultaneously realize a strong economy, sustainable public finances, and a high-quality all-generation social security system.",""],[1,"6","6","Social Security Benefits and Burden Review","Consider reviewing benefits and burdens.",""],[1,"6","6","Medical and Long-Term Care Provision System","Build a medical and long-term care provision system that enables people to receive the necessary services with confidence.",""],[1,"6","6","Digital, AI and Robotics-Based Health Service Improvement","Improve service quality through the use of digital transformation, AI, and robotics.",""],[1,"6","6","Proactive Preventive Healthcare Initiative","Undertake proactive preventive healthcare.",""],[1,"7","1","Essential Health and Care Services Improvement","Work to maintain, improve efficiency, and enhance the quality of essential services such as medical care and nursing.",""]],"134":[[1,"6","7","Priority Budget Allocation for Regional Resilience and Growth","Accordingly, priority budget allocation will be made to crisis-management investment and growth investment that raise regional resilience and earning capacity.",""],[1,"6","7","Integrated Infrastructure and Industrial Cluster Development","Infrastructure development and industrial clusters will be organically linked.",""],[1,"6","7","Comprehensive Regional Digital Technology Utilization","Regional areas will make thorough use of digital technology.",""],[1,"7","3","Integrated Population Decline Response Measures","Promote measures covering both reversing the declining birthrate trend and restructuring the socio-economic system to respond to population decline.",""],[1,"7","3","Population Strategy Headquarters Promotion Framework","Strengthen the promotion system within the Population Strategy Headquarters, including the Council of Experts.",""],[1,"7","3","Comprehensive Population Strategy Formulation","Proceed with consideration toward formulating a consistent and comprehensive strategy, provisionally called the Population Comprehensive Strategy, by the end of 2026.",""],[1,"7","3","Future Labour Force Needs Assessment","At the same time, examine from multiple perspectives the scale of the future labour force that will be required.",""],[1,"8","4","Regional Future Strategy","The Regional Future Strategy for building strong regional economies",""],[1,"14","3","Regional Future Strategy","In addition to previous regional revitalization efforts, the government will strongly promote the new “Regional Future Strategy,” focused on building strong regional economies.",""],[1,"14","3","National Regional Investment and Infrastructure Promotion","For investments based on this strategy, the government will use the “Strong and Prosperous Japan Investment Framework” and take the lead in implementing bold investment promotion measures and infrastructure development as an integrated package.",""],[1,"14","3","Strategic Regional Industrial Cluster Formation","To leverage the growth potential of local areas and create new industrial foundations, industrial clusters will be strategically formed in each region.",""],[1,"14","4","Regional Future Strategy Support Initiative","Based on the “Regional Future Strategy,” proactive support will be provided toward building strong regional economies.",""],[1,"14","4","Regional Crisis-Management and Growth Investment Initiative","Under the “Strategic Industry Cluster Plan,” crisis-management investment and growth investment undertaken at regional-block level across prefectural boundaries and included in the Public-Private Investment Roadmap will serve as a catalyst.",""]],"135":[[1,"5","6","Crisis-Management Investment Initiative","The government will boldly and strategically advance crisis-management investment to minimize various risks.",""],[1,"8","1","Crisis Management Investment","Position crisis-management investment at the core of the growth strategy and take bold measures.",""],[1,"9","2","Crisis Management Investment","Crisis management investment to strengthen products and technologies that contribute to minimizing various risks and solving social issues, secure autonomy, and supply them domestically and internationally.",""],[1,"8","1","Diplomatic and National Security Strengthening","Establish strong diplomacy and security.",""],[1,"8","1","Public Safety and Security Assurance","Promote the assurance of the public's safety and security as an integrated effort.",""],[1,"8","3","Public-Private Crisis Management Investment Initiative","Boldly and strategically advance crisis management investment jointly between the public and private sectors.",""],[1,"10","1","Cybersecurity Strengthening for a Safe Cyberspace","Strengthening cybersecurity to ensure a safe cyberspace",""]],"136":[[1,"5","6","Strategic Sector Investment Initiative","The government will step forward and, working together with the private sector, promote investment in strategic fields.",""],[1,"5","6","Advanced Technology Growth Investment","The government will boldly and strategically advance growth investment to enable advanced technologies to flourish.",""],[1,"5","6","Startup Promotion and Innovation Hub Initiative","The government will promote startups in order to make Japan one of the world's leading hubs for intellectual creation and innovation.",""],[1,"5","6","Multi-Year Budgeting Reform","The government will correct the harmful effects of the single-year fiscal principle and fundamentally reform the way budgets are prepared.",""],[1,"5","7","Productivity Enhancement through Crisis and Growth Investment","Efforts to improve productivity through technological innovation and improvements in the quality of capital through crisis-management investment and growth investment",""],[1,"5","7","Education and Human Resource Development Programme","Strengthen human resources, which form the foundation of economic strength, through education and human resource development",""],[1,"5","7","Continuous Regulatory and Institutional Reform","Through continuous regulatory and institutional reform, create an environment in which companies can continue to take on challenges in the future and strengthen the country's supply structure",""],[1,"8","1","Domestic Investment and Supply Capacity Expansion","Expand domestic investment, strengthen supply capacity, and raise potential growth.",""],[1,"8","1","Growth Investment Initiative","Position growth investment at the core of the growth strategy and take bold measures.",""],[1,"8","1","Growth Foundation Strengthening Programme","Strengthen the foundations for growth, including energy and resource security, science and technology, and innovation.",""],[1,"8","1","Regional Earning Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen the earning power of regions.",""],[1,"8","1","Human Resources Strengthening Initiative","Strengthen human resources.",""],[1,"8","1","Public-Private Investment Roadmap and Policy Packages","Individual measures will be made concrete through a public-private investment roadmap and related policy packages.",""],[1,"8","2","Domestic Investment Expansion Initiative","Japan will position the realization of 250 trillion yen in domestic investment by fiscal year 2040 as a new public-private target, strengthen public-private cooperation more than before, and work to achieve it.",""],[1,"8","3","Strategic Growth Investment Initiative","Boldly and strategically advance growth investment jointly between the public and private sectors.",""],[1,"8","3","Human Capital Strengthening Initiative","Strengthen human resources in order to raise medium- and long-term growth potential.",""],[1,"8","3","Continuous Regulatory and Institutional Reform Programme","Develop an environment that encourages companies to take on challenges through continuous regulatory and institutional reforms.",""],[1,"9","1","Growth Strategy Measures Implementation","All concrete measures included in the strategy will be steadily put into implementation.",""],[1,"9","1","Public-Private Investment in Strategic Fields","Bold public-private investment will be realized.",""],[1,"9","3","Strategic Products and Technologies Policy Package","Steadily implement the policy packages included in nine public-private investment roadmaps covering 62 major products and technologies across 17 strategic fields.",""],[1,"9","3","Multi-Year Budgetary Support Mechanism","Utilize budgetary measures over multiple fiscal years.",""],[1,"9","3","Public Procurement and Regulatory Reform Demand Creation","Create initial demand through government procurement and regulatory reform.",""],[1,"9","3","End-to-End Research and Development Support","Provide seamless support from research and development through to social implementation.",""],[1,"9","3","Human Resources, Data and Computing Infrastructure Development","Develop the business foundations, including human resources, data, and computing resources.",""],[1,"9","3","Tax and Financial Support for Strategic Industries","Provide bold support through tax and financial measures.",""],[1,"9","4","Strategic Portfolio Management and Adaptive Support Measures","Taking the entire range of strategic fields as a portfolio, strategically manage it and adjust support measures in response to changes in circumstances through a multifaceted approach.",""],[1,"9","5","Integrated Infrastructure Development for Domestic Investment","Comprehensively and integrally promote infrastructure development that contributes to promoting domestic investment through behavioral change by both the public and private sectors.",""],[1,"10","1","Domestic Investment Promotion Infrastructure","Establishing the foundations for promoting domestic investment through behavioral change by both the public and private sectors",""],[1,"10","1","Global and Local Industry Productivity Enhancement","Strengthening the competitiveness of global industries and improving the productivity of local industries",""],[1,"10","1","Growth Investment Risk Capital and Finance Enhancement","Strengthening the supply of risk capital supporting growth investment and upgrading financial functions",""],[1,"10","2","Government-Wide Investment and Fiscal Planning Mechanism","Based on the public-private investment roadmaps in the 17 strategic fields specified by the Council for Japan's Growth Strategy, measures and investment amounts addressing eight cross-cutting issues, and estimates of investment amounts, GDP, and the debt-to-GDP ratio, clearly connect crisis-management investment and growth investment to government-wide budget formulation and fiscal management.",""],[1,"10","3","Multi-Year Predictable Investment Support Measures","Utilize predictable investment support measures over multiple fiscal years.",""]],"137":[[1,"7","2","Integrated AI and Human Resources Development Initiative","Advance AI utilization together with human-resource development, securing, mobility, and the full participation of all human resources.",""],[1,"8","4","Advanced Technology Social Implementation Initiative","While emphasizing the realization of the social implementation of advanced technologies",""],[1,"9","2","Advanced Technology Growth Investment","Growth investment to achieve the early social implementation of advanced technologies such as AI and quantum technology in Japan and their expansion into overseas markets, thereby driving innovation-led sustainable growth.",""],[1,"9","2","Cross-Industry AI Transformation Acceleration","Accelerate AI Transformation (AX) across all industries, centered on building physical AI that makes maximum use of Japan's strengths, including abundant field data and manufacturing foundations, to transform toward an economic structure that generates high added value even amid population decline.",""],[1,"11","4","Artificial Intelligence Legal and Guideline Reform","Proactively and radically review laws and guidelines concerning the development and utilization of AI.",""],[1,"11","4","Cross-Ministry AX and DX Implementation Mechanism","Execute AX/DX across ministries as one unified effort.",""],[1,"11","5","Artificial Intelligence Development and Utilization Programme","Strengthen AI development and utilization under appropriate risk management.",""],[1,"11","5","AI and Data Infrastructure Development","Develop AI and data infrastructure while establishing open AI sovereignty.",""],[1,"11","5","Comprehensive AI Governance and Cooperation Capacity Expansion","Work on a drastic expansion of the system for strongly promoting responses including AI-related legal systems, technology, and international cooperation.",""],[1,"11","6","Reliable Data Utilization Enabling Environment","Develop an environment for the utilization of reliable data.",""],[1,"11","6","Government Digital Infrastructure Resilience and Autonomy Strengthening","Strengthen the resilience and improve the autonomy of the government's digital infrastructure.",""],[1,"11","6","Digital Administrative and Fiscal Reform","Advance digital administrative and fiscal reform.",""],[1,"12","3","Cross-Ministry Regulatory Reform Acceleration","Strengthen cross-ministry coordination while working to accelerate institutional revisions through more efficient information collection and analysis, earlier studies and demonstrations, active use of regulatory reform-related systems, and advance setting of review deadlines.",""],[1,"12","3","AI and Drone Technology Social Implementation","Promote the social implementation of new technologies such as AI and drones.",""],[1,"12","3","Integrated Medical Data Use Institutional Design","Promote integrated institutional design for the primary and secondary use of medical and other data.",""]],"138":[[1,"8","4","Regulatory Reform Implementation Plan","The Regulatory Reform Implementation Plan showing the roadmap for regulatory reform",""],[1,"12","2","Regulatory Reform Implementation Plan","The Regulatory Reform Implementation Plan will be strongly promoted.",""],[1,"10","3","Long-Term Investment Research and Regulatory Reform Promotion","Encourage each ministry to conceive, propose, and implement large-scale investments, research and development, and regulatory and institutional reforms from a medium- to long-term perspective.",""],[1,"10","5","Integrated Regulatory and Administrative Reform","Advancing regulatory reform and administrative reform in an integrated manner to eliminate constraints that hinder public- and private-sector investment",""],[1,"10","5","Policy Effects Visualization Mechanism","Promoting the visualization of policy effects",""],[1,"10","5","Good Practice Scaling Mechanism","Promoting the horizontal expansion of good practices",""],[1,"10","6","Industrial Technology Law and R&D Tax Incentive Implementation","Promote the active use of the strengthened R&D tax system and ensure the smooth implementation of the amended Industrial Technology Enhancement Act.",""],[1,"10","7","Partial Amendment to the Industrial Technology Enhancement Act","Act Partially Amending the Industrial Technology Enhancement Act",""],[1,"12","3","Regulatory Reform Promotion Council Secretariat Strengthening","Enhance the organizational structure of the secretariat of the Regulatory Reform Promotion Council while conducting new discussions that contribute to the growth strategy and thoroughly implementing user-oriented regulatory and institutional reform in line with changes in the times and environment and the evolution of technology.",""],[1,"12","3","Local Rule Regulatory Review","Promote the review of local rules.",""],[1,"12","4","Corporate Governance Code and Growth Investment Guidance Implementation","Promote the dissemination and implementation of the revised “Corporate Governance Code” and “Growth Investment Guidance” so that both companies and institutional investors focus on improving corporate value over the medium to long term and are encouraged to undertake necessary growth investments and review their business portfolios.",""],[1,"13","1","Company Law and Shareholder Meeting Review","Consider reviewing the company law system, including the nature of shareholders' meetings.",""],[1,"13","2","Intellectual Property and Intangible Asset Strategy Promotion","Based on the Intellectual Property Promotion Plan 2026, promote the utilization, protection, and standardization of intellectual property and intangible assets through national strategies and business management.",""],[1,"13","2","Cross-Ministry Intellectual Property Coordination Reform","Under the Intellectual Property Strategy Headquarters, which performs the command-center function, work to radically strengthen the organizational structure of the secretariat, including establishing a system to coordinate standardization measures across ministries and agencies.",""]],"139":[[1,"12","1","Space Infrastructure and Strategic Technology Investment","Promote the Space Strategy Fund, quasi-zenith satellites, and the development of JAXA facilities and equipment.",""],[1,"12","1","Space Transportation, Communications and Data Utilization Promotion","Promote space transportation, communications, and data utilization.",""],[1,"12","1","Space Regulatory Review and Examination System","Work on reviewing systems under relevant laws and developing an examination system.",""],[1,"12","1","Space Development Strategy Secretariat Strengthening","Enhance the organizational structure of the secretariat under the Space Development Strategy Headquarters, which performs the command-and-control function.",""],[1,"12","1","Revision of the Basic Plan for Space","Begin revising the Basic Plan for Space.",""],[1,"12","1","Comprehensive Low-Water-Line Conservation Programme","Comprehensively promote initiatives including low-water-line conservation.",""],[1,"12","1","Revision of Japan's Arctic Policy","Begin revising Japan's Arctic Policy.",""],[1,"12","1","Ocean Policy Secretariat Strengthening","Enhance the organizational structure of the secretariat under the Headquarters for Ocean Policy, which performs the command-and-control function.",""],[1,"12","1","Inhabited Border Islands Conservation and Community Sustainability Programme","Further enhance and promote measures for the conservation of inhabited border-island regions and the maintenance of their local communities, including the promotion of stay-type tourism and the demonstration and implementation of advanced technologies.",""],[1,"12","5","Arctic Research Vessel International Cooperation","International cooperation using the Arctic research vessel “Mirai II”",""],[1,"12","5","Antarctic Transportation System Construction","Establishment of an Antarctic transportation system using a successor vessel to “Shirase”",""],[1,"12","5","Ultra-Deep-Sea Exploration Vessel Construction","Construction of an ultra-deep-sea exploration mother ship",""]],"140":[[1,"13","5","GX Investment and Energy Transition Initiative","To achieve the 2050 carbon neutrality target and improve the energy self-sufficiency rate, based on the “Growth Strategy” and “Sector-specific Investment Strategy,” bold GX investment will be promoted from the perspective of crisis-management investment, while maximizing the use of decarbonized power sources and promoting fuel conversion to natural gas, etc.",""],[1,"13","5","Renewable Energy Technology Supply Chain Expansion","For renewable energy, on the premise of local understanding and the S+3E principles, supply chains related to perovskite solar cells and next-generation geothermal power generation equipment will be strengthened and deployment expanded.",""],[1,"13","6","Nuclear Reactor Restart Acceleration","Work to accelerate reactor restarts, with ensuring safety and understanding of local communities as the foremost premises.",""],[1,"13","6","Next-Generation Innovative Reactor Development and Installation","Work to develop and install next-generation innovative reactors.",""],[1,"13","6","Fusion Energy Early Social Implementation","Aim for the early social implementation of fusion energy, ahead of the rest of the world.",""],[1,"13","6","Regional Nuclear Disaster Prevention Capacity Enhancement","Enhance the nuclear disaster prevention system according to regional circumstances, including the development of evacuation roads.",""],[1,"13","6","Final Disposal Survey Area Expansion","Work to expand the surveyed areas related to final disposal.",""],[1,"13","6","Nuclear Safety and Safeguards Framework Strengthening","Consider reviewing safety regulations and establishing an independent administrative agency, among other measures, to strengthen the safeguards framework in anticipation of the operation of reprocessing facilities.",""],[1,"14","1","Asia Zero Emission Community","Through the Asia Zero Emission Community (AZEC), contributing to decarbonization in Asia while incorporating Asia's growth potential.",""]],"141":[[1,"14","4","Regional Industrial Infrastructure Development","Infrastructure development supporting this investment will be boldly advanced.",""],[1,"14","4","Private Industrial Cluster Hub Development","The development of private cluster hubs such as railways, shipbuilding docks, and rocket launch sites will be boldly advanced.",""],[1,"14","4","Supply-Chain Related Enterprise Investment Support","Investment support for related companies in the supply chains forming the clusters will be boldly advanced.",""],[1,"14","5","Regional Industry Cluster and Local Industry Growth Plans","Strongly promote the “Regional Industry Cluster Plans” and “Local Industry Growth Plans” based on ideas originating in the regions.",""],[1,"14","5","Regional Future Grant Expansion","Expand the “Regional Future Grant” to strongly promote the Regional Industry Cluster Plans and Local Industry Growth Plans.",""],[1,"14","5","Regional Growth Financing and Enterprise Support","Advance the integrated provision of growth financing and enterprise support.",""],[1,"14","5","Regional Infrastructure Development Investment","Advance infrastructure development as part of an integrated package.",""],[1,"14","5","Special-Zone Regulatory and Institutional Reform","Advance regulatory and institutional reform by utilizing special-zone systems.",""],[1,"14","5","Industrial Workforce Development Programme","Advance industrial workforce development as part of an integrated package.",""],[1,"14","5","Market Access and Management Support Programme","Advance soft support for expanding sales channels and improving management capabilities.",""],[1,"14","5","Enterprise Equipment Investment Subsidy Utilization","Actively utilize equipment investment subsidies for mid-sized and small and medium-sized enterprises to support the growth investment of regional companies.",""],[1,"14","5","Regional Workforce Development Support","Actively utilize human resources development support measures to support the growth investment of regional companies.",""],[1,"14","5","Regional Foundation Reconstruction Initiative","Under population decline, work to reconstruct regional foundations so that resources can be allocated to growth sectors.",""]],"142":[[1,"14","6","Regional AI Adoption and Digital Transformation Initiative","Promote AI adoption among mid-sized and core regional companies and advance regional AX.",""],[1,"14","6","Regional Youth Education and Employment Support Initiative","Based on the implementation status of the Regional University and Industrial Creation Law, support the promotion of young people pursuing education and employment in the regions.",""]],"143":[[1,"15","1","Domestic Investment Map Monitoring and Publication","The \"Domestic Investment Map,\" which provides a detailed understanding and public disclosure of the extent to which investment has progressed in each region, will be revised and presented regularly.",""],[1,"15","1","Individual Plan 5W1H and PDCA Implementation","In individual plans, the 5W1H—meaning the significance and content of measures, deadlines, responsible departments, forums for consideration, and methods of implementation—will be clarified toward achieving numerical targets, and the PDCA cycle will be thoroughly implemented.",""],[1,"15","1","Government Advisory System for Local Governments","A system will be established in which the government as a whole, including local government agencies, provides advice suited to the needs of local governments.",""]],"144":[[1,"15","3","Yokohama Green Expo 42 Green Technology Fair","Ensure the success of Yokohama Green Expo 42 through an all-Japan system of close public-private collaboration and make it an industrial trade fair for green technologies.",""]],"145":[[1,"15","6","Support Strategy for Transforming SMEs and Mid-Sized Enterprises","Based on the \"Strategy for Strengthening the Earning Power of Mid-Sized and Small and Medium-Sized Enterprises in a Society with Labor Supply Constraints,\" proactive and broad support will be provided to companies taking on transformation.",""],[1,"15","6","Labor-Saving Investment Promotion and Business Support System","By enhancing and promoting the use of various subsidies and grants and cross-industry support systems, the \"Labor-Saving Investment Promotion Plan\" will be steadily implemented, while being further enhanced and expanded.",""]],"146":[[1,"16","4","Industry Promotion through Industry-Academia-Government Collaboration","Industry promotion through industry-academia-government collaboration by the Okinawa Institute of Science and Technology Graduate University",""],[1,"16","4","GW2050 PROJECTS Early Implementation","Early realization of the GW2050 PROJECTS",""],[1,"16","4","Northern and Remote Island Regional Development","Promotion of the northern and remote island regions",""],[1,"16","5","Hokkaido Development Promotion","Promote Hokkaido development, which plays an important role in advancing the Regional Future Strategy.",""],[1,"16","5","Food, Tourism and Zero-Carbon Production Space Development","Maintain and develop production spaces that support food, tourism, and Zero-Carbon Hokkaido.",""],[1,"16","5","GX, AI and DX Industry Cluster Promotion","Promote the accumulation of GX, AI, and DX industries.",""],[1,"16","5","Northern Territories Adjacent Area Development","Advance stable development across the Northern Territories adjacent areas as an integrated region.",""],[1,"16","5","Upopoy Enhancement Initiative","Enhance Upopoy.",""]],"147":[[1,"16","4","Child Poverty Reduction Measures","Efforts toward addressing child poverty",""],[1,"16","4","Well-Being Promotion Initiatives","Initiatives toward realizing well-being",""]],"148":[[1,"16","6","Disadvantaged Areas Support and Transport Gap Elimination Policy","Address measures for disadvantaged areas such as depopulated regions, remote islands, Amami, Ogasawara, peninsulas, and heavy snowfall areas. (Formation of a sustainable and vibrant national territory and elimination of \"transportation blank spots\")",""],[1,"16","10","Regional Transport Resource Utilization Programme","Deepen and accelerate efforts to eliminate “transportation gaps” through the maximum utilization of regional transport resources",""],[1,"16","10","Regional Transport Digital Transformation","Regional transportation digital transformation",""],[1,"16","10","Regional Transport Regulatory Reform","Regulatory reform",""],[1,"17","1","Autonomous Driving Society Development Initiative","Work toward the early realization of an autonomous-driving society and the elimination of mobility shortages.",""]],"149":[[1,"16","9","Water Cycle Restoration and Resource Utilization","Promote the maintenance and recovery of a sound water cycle and the effective utilization of water resources.",""],[1,"16","9","Integrated Basin Water Management and Flood Control","Promote integrated basin-wide water management combining hard and soft measures, and work to accelerate and deepen basin flood control, drought measures, water use including power generation, and the conservation and creation of the basin environment.",""]],"150":[[1,"17","2","Integrated High-Standard Transport Network Development","Promote the early development and utilization of high-standard roads, Development Shinkansen, Chuo Shinkansen Maglev, urban railways, ports, airports, and other logistics and passenger transport networks.",""],[1,"17","2","Traffic Congestion and Modal Connectivity Measures","Promote traffic congestion measures and strengthen modal connectivity.",""],[1,"17","2","Air and Maritime Network Maintenance and Activation","Promote the maintenance and activation of air and maritime networks.",""],[1,"17","2","Transport Sector Workforce Development","Work to secure and train the personnel needed to support these initiatives.",""],[1,"17","2","Narita Airport and Regional Export Hub Development","Advance the enhancement of Narita Airport functions, road and railway access development, surrounding industrial agglomeration, and the development of an export hub for agricultural, forestry, and fishery products across ministries.",""],[1,"17","2","International Airport Access Railway Development","Promote the development of other international airport access railways.",""],[1,"17","2","Conventional Railway Speed Improvement","Promote the speeding-up of conventional railway lines.",""],[1,"17","2","Railway Route Planning Case Studies","Deepen consideration through case studies of routes included in the basic plan.",""],[1,"17","2","Local Railway Restructuring","Promote the restructuring of local railways.",""],[1,"17","2","Railway Network Financing Mechanism","Promote securing financial resources for the railway network.",""],[1,"17","2","Cashless Bus Services","Promote cashless payments for buses.",""],[1,"17","2","Cycling Environment Development","Promote the development and utilization of a favorable environment for bicycle use.",""],[1,"17","7","Early Development of Unstarted Transport Sections","Necessary surveys and other work will be advanced, and efforts will be made toward the early development of sections not yet under construction.",""],[1,"17","7","Support for Early Completion of the Transport Line","In cooperation with municipalities along the line, necessary guidance and technical support will be provided toward opening the entire line as early as possible, also taking into account support through fiscal investment and loans, with the earliest full opening targeted for 2037.",""]],"151":[[1,"17","2","Low-Carbon Logistics Efficiency Programme","Accelerate logistics efficiency and decarbonization through new modal shifts across land, sea, and air, relay transport, and automated logistics roads.",""]],"152":[[1,"17","4","Food Security Strengthening Initiative","We will work to strengthen food security so that citizens can secure safe and nutritionally high-quality food at any time.",""],[1,"17","4","Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries Promotion","We will work to promote agriculture, forestry and fisheries, which form the foundation of food security.",""],[1,"17","6","Agricultural Policy Budget and Implementation System","Secure necessary and sufficient earmarked budgets through agile and flexible responses, strengthen and review measures, and secure a system for promoting measures, including at the local level.",""],[1,"17","6","Farmland Large-Scale Parcel Consolidation","Intensively and systematically promote the creation of large-scale farmland parcels to improve productivity.",""],[1,"17","6","Detailed Infrastructure Development in Hilly and Mountainous Areas","Intensively and systematically promote detailed development in hilly and mountainous areas to improve productivity.",""],[1,"17","6","Shared-Use Facility Reorganization and Rationalization","Intensively and systematically promote the reorganization and rationalization of shared-use facilities to improve productivity.",""],[1,"17","6","Yield-Based Paddy and Upland Crop Support Policy","From Fiscal Year 2027, establish a new paddy-field policy that promotes productivity improvement through support at unit prices corresponding to yields, regardless of whether production is on paddy fields or upland fields.",""],[1,"17","6","Expansion of Hilly Area Direct Payments","Review the measures by expanding the farmland covered by direct payments for hilly and mountainous areas.",""],[1,"17","6","Push-Based Support for Local Farming and Community Activities","Review the measures through push-based initiatives to enable the continuation of local farming and community activities.",""],[1,"17","6","Regional Plan Revision and Farmland Bank Strengthening","Review regional plans and ensure that the farmland bank performs its functions.",""],[1,"18","1","New Farmer and Agricultural Corporation Recruitment Initiative","Promote securing new farmers and corporations as agricultural leaders.",""],[1,"18","1","Full Utilization of Agricultural Land","Promote the full utilization of rice paddies and fields.",""],[1,"18","2","Land Improvement Promotion","Promote land improvement.",""],[1,"18","2","Food Access Assurance","Secure food access.",""],[1,"18","2","Food and Nutrition Education Promotion","Promote food education.",""],[1,"18","2","Livestock Disease Control Measures","Implement livestock disease control measures.",""],[1,"18","2","Seed and Seedling Production Measures","Implement measures for seed and seedling production.",""],[1,"18","2","Wildlife Damage Control Measures","Implement measures against wildlife damage.",""],[1,"18","2","Urban Agriculture Promotion","Promote urban agriculture.",""],[1,"18","2","Rural Community and Regional Business Co-Creation","Promote co-creation between rural and fishing villages and local businesses.",""],[1,"18","2","Rural, Forest, and Marine Industry Promotion","Promote rural, forest, and marine industries to create a related population.",""]],"153":[[1,"17","5","Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries Investment Promotion","Promote investment in the agriculture, forestry and fisheries sectors to expand domestic and overseas demand and strengthen supply capacity.",""],[1,"17","5","Food Technology Investment and Market Expansion","Promote investment in food technologies such as world-leading plant factories and land-based aquaculture, and their deployment in domestic and overseas markets.",""],[1,"17","5","Smart Agriculture Technology and New Variety Development","Promote the development and implementation of smart technologies and new varieties.",""],[1,"17","5","Export Production Area Development","Promote the development of production areas for export.",""],[1,"17","5","Government-Wide Overseas Distribution Channel Development","Strengthen a government-wide system for developing overseas commercial distribution channels.",""],[1,"17","5","Domestic and Overseas Demand Creation for Japanese Food Products","Work to create and expand domestic and overseas demand for domestically produced agricultural, forestry and fishery products and foods, including rice, non-gluten rice flour and Wagyu beef.",""],[1,"18","2","Food Culture Industry Promotion","Promote the food culture industry.",""]],"154":[[1,"18","2","Green Food System Strategy Acceleration","Accelerate the Green Food System Strategy, including climate change adaptation measures and measures to ensure a stable supply of fertilizer.",""]],"155":[[1,"18","3","Forest Consolidation and Boundary Clarification","Forest consolidation and boundary clarification",""],[1,"18","3","Forestry Road Network Development","Focused road network development in areas suitable for forestry",""],[1,"18","3","Forestry Reforestation Programme","Focused reforestation in areas suitable for forestry",""],[1,"18","3","Smart Forestry Development","Smart forestry",""],[1,"18","3","Forestry Human Resources and Management Entity Development","Development of diverse human resources and management entities",""],[1,"18","3","Forestry Supply Chain Strengthening","Supply chain strengthening",""],[1,"18","3","Domestic Timber Conversion and Wood Utilization Expansion","Conversion to domestic timber and expansion of the use of wood and wood-based new materials",""]],"156":[[1,"18","4","Fisheries Resource Survey and Assessment Improvement","Improving resource surveys and assessments",""],[1,"18","4","Fisheries Collaboration Promotion Initiative","Promoting collaboration and other forms of cooperation",""],[1,"18","4","Transition to New Fisheries Operating Models","Transitioning to new operating models",""],[1,"18","4","Fisheries Management Entity and Workforce Securing Initiative","Securing management entities and people",""],[1,"18","4","Smart Fisheries Development Initiative","Smart fisheries",""],[1,"18","4","Fishing Port and Fishing Ground Infrastructure Development","Fishing port and fishing ground development",""],[1,"18","4","Production Market Consolidation and Functional Strengthening","Consolidating and strengthening the functions of production markets",""],[1,"18","4","Fisheries Processing and Distribution Promotion","Promoting processing and distribution",""],[1,"18","4","Aquaculture Seedling and Feed Development","Developing seedlings and feed",""],[1,"18","4","Strategic Aquaculture Growth Industrialization Programme","Promoting the growth and industrialization of aquaculture as a comprehensive and strategic initiative",""]],"157":[[1,"19","2","Human Resources Development and Retention Initiative","Promote national and regional efforts to develop and secure a broad range of human resources, including those in the 17 strategic fields and essential fields.",""],[1,"19","2","Integrated Education, Industry, and Employment Policy Implementation","Coordinate related policies, including education policy, industrial policy, and employment policy, to promote human resources development seamlessly from start to finish.",""],[1,"19","2","Education Quality Improvement Initiative","Improve the quality of education, which is the foundation of human development.",""],[1,"19","2","Reskilling Opportunities Expansion Programme","In cooperation among industry, academia, and government, expand reskilling opportunities through efforts to clarify the skills and treatment required, develop programmes, reduce the burden of costs, enhance information provision, strengthen university systems, and consider further improving the use of scholarships by working adults.",""],[1,"19","2","Advanced Essential Worker Development Programme","Work to develop advanced essential workers.",""],[1,"19","3","All-Generations Reskilling National Movement","Alongside fostering momentum for skills upgrading and respect for skills, the government will develop the \"All-Generations Reskilling National Movement\".",""],[1,"19","3","Preparation to Host the 2028 WorldSkills International Competition","Alongside this, preparations will be advanced for Japan to host the 2028 WorldSkills International Competition.",""],[1,"19","3","Collaborative Skills-Based Human Resources Development","Efforts to develop human resources through collaboration among skilled workers, industry associations, and others will be promoted.",""]],"158":[[1,"19","4","Employment Insurance System Response Review","Consider how the employment insurance system should respond under constraints on labor supply, with a view to reaching a conclusion by sometime in 2026.",""],[1,"19","4","Flexible and Diverse Work Policy Review","Discuss policy responses concerning working-hours legislation and related matters in the Labour Policy Council from after the summer, in order to realize flexible and diverse ways of working.",""],[1,"19","7","Discretionary Work System Scope Review","Regarding the discretionary work system, consideration will be given to reviewing the scope of application, based fully on workplace realities and the positions of both labor and management, on the premise of measures to prevent abuse, including health protection, prevention of excessively long working hours, and ensuring appropriate treatment.",""],[1,"19","7","Flexible Working Hours System Review","Regarding the variable working hours system, consideration will proceed while taking into account workplace realities that cannot adequately respond to factors beyond workers’ control, as well as securing workers’ time for daily life and predictability.",""],[1,"19","7","Working Time and Telework Protection Review","Consideration will also proceed regarding the legal status of restrictions on consecutive working days and working-time interval systems, the nature of the right to disconnect, health protection for side jobs and multiple employment, and promotion of telework use, based fully on workplace realities and the positions of both labor and management.",""],[1,"19","7","Work Style Reform Consultation Support Expansion","Consultation support by the Work Style Reform Support Centers and labor standards inspection offices will be enhanced promptly, while strengthening cooperation with Yorozu Support Centers and others.",""],[1,"19","7","Labor Standards Guidance and Enforcement Reform","At labor standards inspection offices, while responding strictly to serious and malicious cases, guidance will be promptly reviewed so that it is conducted in accordance with agreements between labor and management concerning working hours and measures to secure workers’ health.",""],[1,"19","7","Working Conditions Monitoring and Follow-Up Mechanism","A format will be prepared in advance for monitoring and data collection so that policy effects after implementation can be verified, and the Ministry of Health, Labour and Welfare and its local branch offices will ensure follow-up.","Ministry of Health, Labour and Welfare"],[1,"20","1","Regional Workstyle and Workplace Reform","Also support related efforts by local governments through initiatives such as “Regional Workstyle and Workplace Reform.”",""],[1,"20","1","Employment Ice Age Generation Support Programme","Work to implement the “New Support Programme” to promote employment and improved treatment and social participation for the Employment Ice Age generation and others.",""]],"159":[[1,"20","2","Loneliness and Social Isolation Prevention Support for NPOs","Support NPOs and others working on measures such as creating places and connections, with an emphasis on prevention, in line with the Priority Plan, as measures against loneliness and social isolation.",""],[1,"20","2","New Adult Guardianship System Promotion","Promote the proper implementation of the new adult guardianship system.",""],[1,"20","2","Regional Rights Protection Support System","Ensure a regional rights protection support system.",""],[1,"20","2","Support for Unaccompanied Older People and Other Vulnerable Groups","Provide support for older people without family or relatives, people experiencing social withdrawal, and women facing difficult problems.",""],[1,"20","2","Livelihood Independence Support System","Promote the community-based inclusive society, including the livelihood independence support system.",""],[1,"20","2","Suicide Prevention Measures","Promote the community-based inclusive society, including suicide prevention measures.",""],[1,"20","2","Disability Independence and Social Participation Measures","Implement measures for the independence and social participation of persons with disabilities.",""],[1,"20","3","Compensation Payments under the Former Eugenic Protection Law","Steadily advance the payment of compensation payments, etc. under the former Eugenic Protection Law.",""],[1,"20","7","Loneliness and Social Isolation Prevention Initiatives","Implement initiatives to prevent loneliness and isolation by responding before worries and difficulties become serious or complex.",""],[1,"20","7","Comprehensive Suicide Prevention Measures","Measures based on the Comprehensive Suicide Prevention Policy Outline, aiming to realize a society in which no one is driven to suicide.",""],[1,"20","7","Disability Inclusion and Sign Language Measures","Measures based on the Action Plan for Realizing an Inclusive Society Without Prejudice or Discrimination Against Persons with Disabilities, the Fifth Basic Plan for Persons with Disabilities, and the Act on the Promotion of Measures Related to Sign Language.",""],[1,"20","7","Compensation Payments for Eugenic Surgery Victims","Compensation payments, lump-sum payments for eugenic surgery, and lump-sum payments for induced abortion under the Act on the Provision of Compensation Payments and Other Benefits to Persons Who Underwent Eugenic Surgery, etc., Based on the Former Eugenic Protection Law.",""]],"160":[[1,"22","2","Defense Production Base Enhancement Act Review","Review of the Defense Production Base Enhancement Act is also being considered.",""],[1,"22","2","State Involvement in Critical Equipment Supply","Consideration is being given to national involvement, including GOCO, in important equipment whose stable supply is difficult.",""],[1,"22","2","Defense Equipment Production Capacity Expansion","Consideration is being given to strengthening increased production capacity on the premise of peacetime use for civilian products and equipment transfers.",""],[1,"22","2","Defense Equipment Transfer Support Mechanism","Consideration is being given to government-led transfers, financing, and accompanying support in equipment transfers, while advancing coordination with relevant organizations.",""],[1,"22","2","Defense Startup Utilization Programme","Further utilization of startups will be promoted.",""],[1,"22","2","Defense Research Infrastructure and Development Programme","Defense research and development will be promoted through the development of a defense research base for national research institutes and universities, thereby rapidly incorporating cutting-edge technology.",""],[1,"22","2","State-Involved Defense Corporation Establishment","Consideration is being given to establishing a corporation that ensures national involvement in order to promote these measures in an integrated manner.",""]],"161":[[1,"22","6","Satellite Constellation Construction Initiative","To strengthen space security, efforts will be undertaken including the construction of a satellite constellation.",""],[1,"22","6","Cyber Response Capability Implementation Framework","A framework will be established to steadily implement the Cyber Response Capability Enhancement Act and other measures.",""],[1,"22","6","National Cyber Information Collection and Response Review","The appropriate methods for information collection and response in cyberspace will be examined from the perspective of national security.",""],[1,"22","6","Government Information Security Capacity Strengthening","The government’s information security system will be strengthened in light of advances in AI performance.",""],[1,"22","6","Secure Government Cloud Introduction","The introduction of cloud services equipped with the information protection and secrecy protection measures necessary to handle highly confidential information will be promoted while ensuring autonomous operation and management.",""],[1,"22","6","National Security Strategy Revision Measures","In light of discussions concerning the revision of the National Security Strategy, necessary measures will be considered.",""],[1,"23","7","Sensitive Personal Data Protection Bill","The government aims to submit at an early date a bill on protecting sensitive personal data important to national security.",""],[1,"23","7","Data Centre and Cloud Security Measures","The government will take necessary measures to ensure the security of data centres and cloud services.",""],[1,"23","7","Critical Infrastructure Cybersecurity Strengthening","The government will strengthen the cybersecurity of critical infrastructure operators and others in light of advances in AI performance.",""],[1,"23","7","Software Vulnerability Detection and Response Capacity","The government will improve vendors' ability to detect and respond to software vulnerabilities at an early stage.",""]],"162":[[1,"22","7","Intelligence Capability Strengthening Reform","Fundamentally strengthen intelligence functions that support the maintenance of sound democracy, smooth government decision-making, and external communications amid the most severe and complex security environment since the end of the war.",""],[1,"22","8","External Intelligence Collection Capacity Enhancement","Enhance and strengthen external intelligence collection functions",""],[1,"22","8","AI-Enabled Intelligence Communications Infrastructure","Develop information and communications infrastructure utilizing AI and other technologies",""],[1,"22","8","Intelligence Personnel Development Programme","Promote human resources development",""],[1,"22","8","Inter-Ministerial Intelligence Support System Strengthening","Strengthen as soon as practicable the systems of the relevant ministries supporting these activities, including the system for collecting human intelligence",""],[1,"22","9","Integrated National Core Functions Coordination System","The Cabinet Secretariat, Cabinet Office, police, and Ministry of Defense/Self-Defense Forces will jointly develop a system to undertake core functions.","Cabinet Secretariat | Cabinet Office | Ministry of Defense/Self-Defense Forces"],[1,"23","1","External Information Collection Organizational Review","Proceed with examining effective organizational arrangements for collecting external information.",""],[1,"23","1","Information-Gathering Satellite Expansion","By steadily increasing the number of information-gathering satellites, further expansion and strengthening of capabilities will be pursued.",""],[1,"23","2","Foreign Influence Information Analysis Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen information-gathering and analysis capabilities concerning influence operations from abroad, including the spread of disinformation that threatens the foundations of democracy, such as fair elections and free reporting.",""],[1,"23","3","Multilingual Strategic Communications and Expert Collaboration","To counter cognitive warfare, fundamentally strengthen accurate multilingual communications and effective, strategic communications in cooperation with experts and influential think tanks in Japan and abroad.",""],[1,"23","3","Historical Recognition and Territorial Sovereignty Research","Fundamentally strengthen research and domestic and international communications on historical recognition, territories, and sovereignty.",""],[1,"23","4","Government-Wide Economic Security Promotion System","For these purposes, the government-wide promotion system, with the National Security Secretariat as its command center, will be strengthened.","National Security Secretariat"]],"163":[[1,"24","1","Cross-Ministerial Investment Review System Strengthening","Drastically strengthen the cross-ministerial review system.",""],[1,"24","1","Foreign Investment Screening Enhancement","Work to enhance investment screening based on the revised Foreign Exchange and Foreign Trade Act.",""],[1,"24","1","Critical Technology Management Measures","Take institutional measures to strengthen the management of important technologies from the perspective of economic security.",""],[1,"24","1","Research Security and Integrity Assurance","Ensure research security and integrity.",""],[1,"24","1","International Researcher Admission Screening","Strengthen screening for the acceptance of international students and foreign researchers.",""],[1,"24","1","Economic Coercion and Sanctions Response","Strengthen responses to economic coercion and various sanctions.",""],[1,"24","1","Export Controls and Trade Remedies Enhancement","Work to strengthen export controls and enhance the effectiveness of trade remedy measures.",""]],"164":[[1,"26","4","Pharmaceuticals and Medical Devices Research and Security Programme","Promote research and development and securing pharmaceuticals and medical devices.",""],[1,"26","4","Post-COVID Symptoms and Vaccine Reaction Research","Promote research on post-COVID-19 symptoms and adverse reactions to vaccines.",""],[1,"26","4","One Health Zoonotic Disease Control Measures","Promote measures against zoonotic infectious diseases through One Health.",""],[1,"26","7","Emergency Response Medicine Production and Stockpiling","Strengthening the production system and stockpiling of emergency response medicines.",""]],"165":[[1,"26","5","Climate Change Adaptation Measures Implementation","Social implementation of climate change adaptation measures such as heatstroke prevention",""],[1,"26","5","Nature-Positive Biodiversity Conservation","Biodiversity conservation through the realization of nature positive",""],[1,"26","5","Environmental and Livelihood Risk Response Measures","Advance responses to risks related to the living environment, natural environment, and livelihoods, including bear damage, invasive species, hay fever, PFAS, and soil contamination",""]],"166":[[1,"26","7","Emergency Response to Bear Appearances","Continue efforts including emergency response when bears appear.",""],[1,"26","7","Prevention of Bear Encroachment into Human Living Areas","Prevention of bears appearing in people's living areas.",""],[1,"26","7","Bear Population Management","Strengthening population management.",""]],"167":[[1,"27","1","Immigration Services Agency Capacity Strengthening","As a priority, fundamentally strengthen the human and material systems of the Immigration Services Agency.","Immigration Services Agency"],[1,"27","1","JESTA Introduction Preparation","Advance preparatory work toward the introduction of JESTA during fiscal year 2028.","Immigration Services Agency"],[1,"27","1","Digital Transformation of Immigration Screening","Promote digital transformation to make screening faster and more sophisticated.","Immigration Services Agency"],[1,"27","1","Zero Illegal Stay Plan","Strongly promote the Zero Illegal Stay Plan and further ensure the proper administration of immigration control.","Immigration Services Agency"],[1,"27","1","Employment for Skill Development Implementation and Illegal Employment Control","Develop the necessary systems for the smooth implementation of the Employment for Skill Development System and measures against illegal employment.","Immigration Services Agency"],[1,"27","1","Private Lodging Operations Regulation","Thoroughly ensure the proper operation of various private lodging facilities.",""],[1,"27","5","Zero Illegal Residents Plan and Strong Promotion Package","“Zero Illegal Residents Plan—Strong Promotion Package” (announced May 22, 2026).",""]],"168":[[1,"27","2","Foreign Resident Japanese and Civic Education Strengthening","Strengthen education in Japanese and in Japan's systems and rules so that foreign nationals can act responsibly as members of Japanese society.",""],[1,"27","2","Japanese Language and Life Learning Programme","Begin efforts toward the creation of the Japanese Language and Life Learning Programme (tentative).",""],[1,"27","2","Nationwide Pre-Class Expansion","Begin efforts toward the nationwide expansion of pre-classes.",""],[1,"27","2","Registered Japanese Language Teacher Treatment Improvement","Begin efforts to improve the treatment of registered Japanese language teachers.",""],[1,"27","2","Regional and School Support System Development","Develop systems in regions and schools.",""],[1,"27","3","Basic Policy on the Acceptance of Foreign Nationals","Begin discussions in an expert panel on the basic approach to accepting foreign nationals and compile a basic policy during fiscal year 2026.",""]],"169":[[1,"27","4","Foreign Land Acquisition Rules Framework","Compile the basic framework of rules on foreign nationals' acquisition of land, etc., by summer 2026.",""],[1,"27","4","Important Land Survey Act Enforcement Strengthening","Strengthen the enforcement system for the Act on Important Land and Related Survey, including land surveys and use regulations.",""],[1,"27","4","Groundwater Conservation and Use Management Mechanism","Develop a mechanism to ensure the proper conservation and use of groundwater.",""],[1,"27","4","Land Acquisition Information and Oversight System","Consider, including legislation, a system to strengthen information gathering and oversight concerning the acquisition and use of land.",""]],"170":[[1,"28","2","Private Investment Expansion and Supply Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen supply capacity through expanded private investment, link this to economic growth and a stronger tax base, and achieve a strong economy and fiscal sustainability together.",""],[1,"28","3","Growth Strategy for Supply Capacity Strengthening","Promote the “Growth Strategy,” centered on crisis-management investment and growth investment, strongly to strengthen supply capacity.",""],[1,"28","3","Public-Private Investment Mobilization","The government will also step forward and advance the realization of public-private investment.",""],[1,"28","3","Investment Environment Development","The government will also step forward and advance the concrete development of the investment environment.",""],[1,"28","3","Regional Future Strategy Implementation","Execute the “Regional Future Strategy” to build strong regional economies.",""],[1,"28","3","New Regional Industrial Base Development","Build new industrial foundations by leveraging the growth potential of local areas.",""],[1,"28","4","Public-Private Crisis and Growth Investment Promotion","Based on the Public-Private Investment Roadmap, promote crisis-management investment and growth investment.",""],[1,"28","4","Research and Development and Production Resource Efficiency Measures","In addition to such public-private investment, investment in research and development and the more efficient allocation of production resources will be pursued.",""],[1,"28","5","Strong and Prosperous Japan Investment Framework","The creation of the “Strong and Prosperous Japan” Investment Framework",""],[1,"30","1","Strong and Prosperous Japan Investment Framework","Creation of the “Strong and Prosperous Japan” Investment Framework.",""],[1,"30","2","Strong and Prosperous Japan Investment Framework","To enable measures that raise potential growth through domestic investment, including crisis-management investment and growth investment, to be implemented predictably, the “Strong and Prosperous Japan” investment framework will be established separately from ordinary expenditures.",""],[1,"42","2","Strong and Prosperous Japan Investment Framework","A “Strong and Prosperous Japan” investment framework will be established separately from ordinary expenditures, including crisis-management and growth investments, so that measures contributing to raising potential growth through domestic investment can be implemented predictably.",""],[1,"42","4","Strong and Prosperous Japan Investment Framework","The Strong and Prosperous Japan Investment Framework, including crisis-management investment and growth investment, will target measures with a strong effect on substantially increasing domestic private capital investment and potential growth.",""],[1,"30","4","Public-Private Investment Roadmap Implementation and Private Investment Mobilization","This will secure the scale and period necessary for the steady implementation of the public-private investment roadmap, draw out private investment, and lead to strengthening supply capacity and the tax revenue base.",""],[1,"31","2","Multi-Year Financing Mechanism for Strategic Investments","Use funds, multi-year contracts through multi-year obligations, fiscal investment and loans, and equity contributions, while strengthening governance.",""]],"171":[[1,"28","4","Government Budget-Making Reform","The government will fundamentally reform the way it prepares its budgets so that truly effective policies based on new ideas and perspectives, including those from the private sector, can be elicited while overcoming the extensions and constraints of conventional policies.",""],[1,"28","5","Growth-Oriented Budget Formulation Reform","A shift to budget formulation appropriate for strengthening economic growth and expanding the nominal size of the economy",""],[1,"29","9","Growth-Oriented Budget Formulation Reform","In the budget formulation process, the contribution to growth and the effect of inducing private investment will be carefully examined, transforming Japan's budget into one that contributes to strengthening growth potential.",""],[1,"28","5","Reduction of Supplementary Budget Dependence","Breaking away from dependence on supplementary budgets",""],[1,"28","5","Review of Funds and Multi-Year Budget Measures","Reviewing the way budgets are formulated, including funds and budgetary measures extending over multiple years",""],[1,"28","5","Fiscal Analysis and Verification Strengthening","Strengthening analysis and verification to secure market confidence",""],[1,"29","9","Special Tax Measures and Subsidies Review","Inspection and review of special tax measures and subsidies will be advanced, policy priorities will be re-examined, and resources will be boldly focused.",""],[1,"29","10","Evidence-Based Review of Non-Social-Security Expenditure","For non-social-security expenditures, while appropriately reflecting rises in prices and wages, existing programmes will be addressed based on PDCA and EBPM in accordance with the policy described above.",""],[1,"29","11","Ministry Budget Request Review Mechanism","In reviewing the measures, each ministry will submit its budget request reflecting its self-inspection, and the content of the review will be scrutinized during the budget formulation process before being made concrete.",""],[1,"30","3","Effective Investment Budgeting Support Mechanism","A mechanism will be established to link the budget formulation process to effective budget measures, enabling appropriate requests for the necessary amounts, including item requests, without setting a request ceiling, regardless of the previous fiscal year's budgetary measures.",""],[1,"30","6","Supplementary Budget and Multi-Year Budget Reform","Breaking away from dependence on supplementary budgets and reviewing funds and budgetary measures spanning multiple fiscal years",""],[1,"30","7","Fiscal Budgeting Reform to Limit Supplementary Budget Dependence","Break away from fiscal management that has continued to depend on supplementary budgets based on large-scale economic measures, limit supplementary budgets to highly urgent items, and provide for permanent measures in the initial budget.",""],[1,"30","8","Multi-Year Budget and Fund Management Reform","Funds and multi-year budgetary measures will be reviewed to reconcile the predictability needed for long-term investment with flexible and efficient financial management.",""],[1,"31","1","Fund Rules Fundamental Review","Including non-application of the current rule that budgetary measures are, in principle, limited to within three years, concretize a fundamental review of fund rules toward the FY2027 budget formulation.",""],[1,"42","4","FY2027 Ministry Budget Request Process","In the FY2027 budget formulation, each ministry and agency shall submit appropriate budget requests based on the above.",""],[1,"42","4","Supplementary and Initial Budget Classification Framework","The budget formulation process will clarify the principles for distinguishing supplementary budgets from initial budgets.",""]],"172":[[1,"31","6","Integrated Social Security and Tax Reform","Promoting integrated reform of social security and taxation (tax system reform)",""],[1,"31","7","Comprehensive Tax System Reform Review","Under responsible active fiscal policy, comprehensive consideration will be advanced toward concretizing an appropriate tax system that responds to structural changes in the economic and social environment, including declining birthrates, population aging, and globalization, while giving sufficient consideration to fiscal sustainability.",""],[1,"31","8","Digital Society Tax System and Tax Payment Environment Reform","Strengthen initiatives from both the institutional and enforcement-structure perspectives to build a tax system suited to a digital society, improve the tax payment environment, and realize appropriate and fair taxation.",""],[1,"31","8","New International Tax Rules Adaptation","Advance responses to new international tax rules.",""],[1,"31","9","Refundable Tax Credit and Interim Consumption Tax Policy","Regarding the refundable tax credit and its interim measure (such as the consumption tax rate on food and beverages), the policy will be decided by early August this year, based on the forthcoming interim report of the Social Security National Council.",""],[1,"29","10","Social Security Benefit and Contribution Reform","Under the policy of stopping and reducing increases in insurance premium rates for the working-age generation, reforms of benefits and burdens will continue, taking into account total benefit expenditure, public and insurance premium burdens, and the disposable income of the working-age generation, not only national government expenditure.",""],[1,"42","1","Social Security Benefits and Contributions Reform","Reform of benefits and burdens will be continued, taking into account total benefit expenditures, public and insurance contributions, and the disposable income of working-age generations.",""]],"173":[[1,"32","1","Sustainable Institutional Design Reform","Institutions must also be changed to sustainable designs in line with a growth-oriented economy.",""],[1,"32","2","Universal Health Insurance and Pension System Maintenance","Maintain universal health insurance and universal pensions.",""],[1,"32","2","All-Generation Social Security System","Build an all-generation social security system in which the necessary services are appropriately provided to those who need them.",""],[1,"32","2","Public Information on Future Social Security","Provide the public, including young people, with easily understandable information about the future shape of all-generation social security, including the overall picture of benefits and contributions.",""],[1,"32","3","Social Security System Reform Programme","Based on the agreed specific outlines for the 13 social security reform items included in the Coalition Government Agreement (October 20, 2025), concrete system design will be undertaken during fiscal year 2026 and implemented sequentially.",""],[1,"32","4","Healthcare, Long-Term Care and Welfare Service Provision System","Establish a system that enables people to receive healthcare, long-term care and welfare services with peace of mind.",""],[1,"32","4","Social Security System and Expenditure Reform","Steadily implement social security system reforms centered on healthcare and long-term care.",""],[1,"32","5","Social Security System Reform","Steadily implement social security system reform.",""],[1,"32","8","Social Security Benefits and Burden Reform","Efforts to reform benefits and burdens will continue for social security-related expenditures.",""]],"174":[[1,"33","1","Comprehensive Physician Maldistribution Measures","Implement comprehensive measures to address the maldistribution of physicians, including the exercise of family doctor functions, further corrective measures for regional and specialty imbalances among physicians, and promotion of physician dispatches from university hospitals and other institutions.",""],[1,"33","1","Medical School Enrollment Adjustment","Work to reduce medical school enrollment quotas from fiscal year 2028 onward, taking regional circumstances into consideration.",""],[1,"33","1","Dental Workforce Distribution Measures","Develop a dental healthcare delivery system, including measures to address the maldistribution of dental professionals.",""],[1,"33","1","Medical Workforce Training and Recruitment Measures","Consider measures for the effective training and recruitment of healthcare personnel.",""],[1,"33","1","Nursing Quality Improvement and Workforce Distribution","Promote measures to improve the quality of nursing staff and address their maldistribution, including the utilization of latent human resources.",""],[1,"33","1","Care and Welfare Workforce Development","Work to train, secure and retain human resources in the long-term care and welfare fields.",""],[1,"33","1","Care and Welfare Workplace and Management Improvement Support","Support operational efficiency, safety measures, improvement of working environments, and collaboration and scaling-up of management in the long-term care and welfare fields.",""],[1,"33","1","Planned Medical Facility and Equipment Development","Consider how necessary support should be provided for the planned development of facilities and equipment indispensable to local communities, including measures for aging infrastructure and disasters, based on future demand under the new community medical care vision.",""],[1,"33","1","Planned Care and Welfare Facility Development","Support the planned development of facilities and equipment in the long-term care and welfare fields, including measures for aging infrastructure and disasters.",""],[1,"33","4","Medical Personnel Specialization Development","Consider approaches to training that maintain and improve the specialization of medical personnel.",""],[1,"33","4","Specified Medical Procedures Training Promotion","Promote training in specified medical procedures.",""],[1,"33","4","Dental Workforce Employment and Retention Measures","Implement employment and turnover measures for dental hygienists and dental technicians.",""],[1,"33","4","Dental Laboratory Quality and Coordination Improvement","Improve the quality of dental laboratories and strengthen their coordination.",""]],"175":[[1,"33","2","Medical Co-Payment Reform for Older People","The system will be reviewed from the perspective of realizing genuinely fair ability-to-pay contributions regardless of age between people aged 70 and over and the working generation, whose principle is a 30 percent co-payment.",""],[1,"33","2","Long-Term Care Co-Payment Criteria Reform","A conclusion will be reached during fiscal year 2026 on reviewing the criteria for determining the 20 percent co-payment under the long-term care insurance system.",""],[1,"33","2","Financial Income and Asset Treatment Reform","Efforts based on the reform roadmap will be advanced, including the treatment of financial income and assets in medical and long-term care insurance.",""],[1,"33","2","OTC-Like Drug Insurance Coverage Reform","The scope will be considered for expansion from fiscal year 2027 onward, taking into account the implementation and status of the review of insurance benefits for OTC-like drugs.",""],[1,"33","2","Biosimilar Uptake and Coverage Reform","The government will consider reviewing the appropriate nature of insurance benefits for originator biopharmaceuticals, taking into account the status of efforts to create an environment conducive to promoting the use of biosimilars.",""],[1,"33","2","Efficient Prescription and Treatment Practices","The provision of high-quality services will be achieved while making benefits more efficient and appropriate by promoting effective and efficient treatment, including the use of long-term prescriptions and refill prescriptions, nationwide expansion of regional formularies, and suspension or reduction of medication.",""],[1,"33","2","Switch to Over-the-Counter Medicines and Tests","Effective measures will be considered and implemented to further promote the switching of medicines and test kits to OTC products from the perspective of promoting self-medication.",""],[1,"33","4","Healthcare Copayment and Public Financing Reform","Comprehensively consider a fundamental review of outpatient special provisions, income thresholds for copayment rates, and raising the applicable age, together with the appropriate form of public financing from the perspective of reducing the burden on the working generation.",""],[1,"33","4","Income and Asset Information Infrastructure Development","Urgently advance the development of an infrastructure for grasping income and asset information by utilizing the My Number system and promote its reflection in the system.",""]],"176":[[1,"34","2","Pension Reserve Management for Future Benefit Security","Manage pension reserves with the aim of exceeding the wage growth rate over the long term and securing future pension benefit levels.",""],[1,"34","2","Medical Assistance Optimization in Public Assistance","Promote the proper provision of medical assistance under public assistance.",""],[1,"34","2","Employment Support Promotion for Public Assistance Recipients","Promote employment support under public assistance.",""],[1,"34","2","Public Assistance Standard Revision Based on Periodic Review","In the revision of the next livelihood assistance standards, make revisions by comprehensively taking into account the consumption realities of general low-income households and socioeconomic conditions based on the results of periodic verification.",""],[1,"33","4","Social Welfare Staff Retirement Mutual Aid Review","Consider the future form of the retirement allowance mutual aid system for social welfare facility staff and others.",""]],"177":[[1,"34","3","Public-Private Investment in Drug Discovery and Advanced Medicine","Expand public-private investment in drug discovery and advanced medicine to achieve health and medical security.",""],[1,"34","3","Innovative Pharmaceutical and Medical Device Development","Create innovative pharmaceuticals, medical devices, and other products.",""],[1,"34","3","Secure Market Launches for Essential Medicines","Develop an environment in which necessary medicines and other products can be reliably launched even amid recent policy developments in other countries concerning pharmaceuticals, such as the United States' most-favored-nation pricing policy for medicines.",""],[1,"34","3","Domestic Production for Stable Medicine Supply","Ensure a stable supply through the domestic production of medicines and other products for which the need to secure supply is high, including specified important goods.",""],[1,"34","3","Advanced Technology Commercialisation Programme","Aim to put advanced technologies into practical use.",""],[1,"34","3","Domestic Biosimilar Production Capacity Development","Steadily advance the development of a domestic production system for biosimilars.",""],[1,"34","3","Industrial Structural Reform for Generic Medicine Supply","Ensure a stable supply of generic medicines and other products by promoting industrial structural reform.",""],[1,"34","4","Drug Discovery and Advanced Medicine Development Policy","Drug discovery and advanced medicine will be comprehensively promoted as a driving force for the growth economy.",""],[1,"34","4","Biomedical Manufacturing and Supply Chain Strengthening","Strengthening research and development capabilities and manufacturing and supply, and reinforcing distribution systems, will be promoted.",""],[1,"34","4","Biomedical Startup Support Programme","Startup support will be promoted.",""],[1,"34","4","Advanced Medicine Human Resources Development","Human resources development will be promoted.",""],[1,"34","4","Advanced Medicine Coverage Expansion","Expansion of the coverage of advanced medicine will be promoted.",""],[1,"34","4","International Expansion of Drug Discovery and Advanced Medicine","International development will be promoted.",""],[1,"34","4","Regenerative Medicine and Priority Medicines Research and Production","Research, development, and production will be promoted for regenerative, cellular, and gene therapies using whole-genome analysis and induced pluripotent stem cells, immunotherapies, medicines for children and rare diseases, radioisotopes, and medicines addressing infectious diseases including antimicrobial-resistant bacteria.",""],[1,"34","4","Artificial Intelligence for Drug and Medical Technology Development","The use of artificial intelligence in drug discovery, medical device development, and diagnosis will be promoted.",""],[1,"34","4","International Clinical Trial System Development","An internationally competitive system for clinical trials and clinical studies will be established.",""],[1,"34","4","Domestic Self-Sufficiency in Plasma-Derived Products","Efforts will be made to achieve domestic self-sufficiency in plasma-derived products.",""],[1,"34","7","Medical Radioisotope Development and Supply System","Regarding radioisotopes, based on the Action Plan for Promoting the Production and Use of Medical Radioisotopes, necessary initiatives will be advanced to establish development, production, stable supply, and medical provision systems.",""],[1,"34","7","Infectious Disease Crisis Medicine Development and Production Reform","Consideration of the necessary legal and institutional systems based on the Strategy for Strengthening Development and Production Systems for Infectious Disease Crisis Response Medicines, including vaccines, therapeutics, and diagnostic medicines.",""],[1,"34","5","2027 Drug Price Revision","Based on an accurate understanding of market prices affected by economic and price trends through drug price surveys and other means, implement the fiscal 2027 drug price revision.",""],[1,"34","5","Cost-Effectiveness Evaluation System Review","Advance objective verification of the cost-effectiveness evaluation system, concretely consider further reviews for the system's development based on this verification, and reach a conclusion.",""],[1,"34","5","Enhanced Evaluation of Innovative New Drug Innovation","Proceed with consideration of further evaluation of innovation in innovative new drugs, including appropriate evaluation at the time of initial listing for breakthrough medicines and the approach to drug prices during the patent period.",""]],"178":[[1,"36","6","Public Education Renewal and Quality Improvement Reform","The Takaichi Cabinet will regenerate public education, the foundation of human development, and fundamentally improve the quality of education.",""],[1,"36","7","Developmentally Appropriate AI Education Programme","Support instruction on the use of AI according to the developmental stages of children and students, and foster human resources capable of navigating an uncertain and rapidly changing society.",""],[1,"36","7","School AI Guidelines Revision","Revise the AI guidelines for schools promptly.",""],[1,"36","7","GIGA School AI Implementation Initiative","Promote the GIGA School Initiative as a national policy, advance environmental development and demonstration research for safe and proactive AI use, and create and disseminate advanced examples.",""],[1,"36","8","Integrated Human Resource Development System Reform","The human resource development system from high school through university and graduate school will be reformed as an integrated whole to strengthen the human resource base in response to changes in the industrial structure.",""],[1,"37","3","Inclusive and Inquiry-Based Learning Environment Development","Develop learning environments aimed at by the next Courses of Study, including inclusion of diversity, a fundamental improvement in information-use skills, and high-quality inquiry based on students’ interests and concerns.",""],[1,"37","3","Bullying and School Non-Attendance Response Measures","Comprehensively advance measures against bullying, school non-attendance, and related issues.",""],[1,"37","3","Special Needs Education Enhancement","Enhance special needs education.",""],[1,"37","3","School Safety Promotion Initiative","Advance school safety initiatives and promote the creation of schools that students can attend with peace of mind.",""],[1,"37","3","School Educational Environment Renewal Support","Provide steady support so that local governments and others can jointly and systematically improve school educational environments and address deterioration, thereby creating creative learning environments.",""],[1,"37","3","Experiential and Reading Activity Promotion","Promote experiential activities and reading activities.",""],[1,"37","3","School-Based Nutrition Education Promotion","Promote food education centered on nutrition teachers.",""],[1,"37","3","School Dental Health Education Promotion","Promote dental health education.",""],[1,"37","3","School-Based Myopia Prevention Programme","Promote myopia prevention.",""],[1,"37","3","Overseas Education Facility Functional Strengthening","Strengthen the functions of overseas education facilities by leveraging their distinctive characteristics.",""]],"179":[[1,"37","1","Higher Education Scale Optimization and Regional Rebalancing","Comprehensively promote scale optimization based on the decline, rebalance higher education fields and regions, and move away from an 18-year-old-centered model.",""],[1,"37","1","University Growth-Field Reorganization and Function Strengthening","Strengthen the functions of universities and graduate schools, including the development of science, technology, engineering, mathematics, and digital talent, through faculty reorganization toward growth fields.",""],[1,"37","1","Strategic Field Advanced Talent and Reskilling Programme","Promote advanced human-resource development in 17 strategic fields and reskilling according to actual demand.",""],[1,"37","1","College of Technology Expansion and Functional Strengthening","Establish new colleges of technology and strengthen their functions.",""],[1,"37","1","International Study Promotion for Students","Further promote overseas study among university and high school students.",""],[1,"37","1","Education Outcomes and Quality Information Disclosure","Strengthen the provision of information on educational outcomes and quality.",""],[1,"37","1","Regional Workforce and Vocational Education Strengthening","Promote the development of high-quality human resources essential for maintaining regional medical care, nursing care, welfare, industry, and infrastructure, as well as the organization of integrated curricula for specialized high schools and junior colleges and the advancement of specialized school education.",""],[1,"37","1","High School Education Reform Fund Support","Promote high school education reform with support from the High School Education Reform Promotion Fund.",""],[1,"37","1","New Fiscal Support Mechanism for High School Reform","Construct new fiscal support mechanisms, including grants, after securing stable financial resources, and promote high school education reform in response to social change.",""],[1,"37","1","Education Cost Burden Reduction","Continue efforts to reduce the burden of education expenses.",""],[1,"37","4","New System for Support for Study","Even amid rising prices, steadily implement the New System for Support for Study.",""],[1,"37","4","Tuition Payment Deferral System","Even amid rising prices, steadily implement the Tuition Payment Deferral System.",""],[1,"37","4","University Reform","Advance university reform.",""],[1,"37","4","Targeted Private School Subsidy Enhancement","Target and enhance private school subsidies toward human resource development supporting growth fields and regions.",""],[1,"37","5","Regional Education Transport Support","This includes securing means of transportation for instructors and students involved in regional deployment.",""],[1,"37","5","AI-Enabled English Education","This includes enhancing English education, including the use of AI.",""],[1,"37","5","Advanced Talent Education Programme","This includes enhancing education to develop the qualities and abilities of children and students with exceptional talents in specific fields.",""],[1,"37","5","School Counseling and Education Support Services","Progress will be made in securing educational opportunities, including developing an environment where students can consult school counselors and school social workers and promoting the establishment of educational support centers inside and outside schools.",""],[1,"37","5","Nationwide Night Junior High School Expansion","In addition, the nationwide establishment of night junior high schools will be promoted.",""]],"180":[[1,"38","5","Strategic Social Infrastructure Development","For the realization of a “strong economy,” it is important to strategically develop social infrastructure that supports crisis-management investment and growth investment.",""],[1,"38","6","Construction Industry Productivity and Workforce Improvement Initiative","Through productivity improvements, including the introduction of physical AI, improvements in treatment such as wage increases, and the development of an environment in which diverse human resources can be secured and play active roles, strengthen the capacity to develop regional infrastructure.",""],[1,"38","6","Stable Public Investment and Construction Cost Pass-Through Policy","While promoting stable and sustainable public investment based on a medium- to long-term outlook, secure the necessary volume of work and advance efficient and focused efforts after encouraging appropriate price pass-through while taking into account the need to secure labor costs and the effects of recent sharp increases in material prices.",""],[1,"38","6","PPP and PFI Promotion Action Plan","Promote public-private partnership investment and other measures based on the PPP/PFI Promotion Action Plan (2026 revised edition).",""],[1,"38","6","Public Works Evaluation and Social Discount Rate Reform","Regarding public works evaluation, revise it toward a comprehensive evaluation that does not rely excessively on cost-benefit ratios and takes into account national strategies, disaster prevention and reduction, national resilience, and basic functions that protect the lives and livelihoods of local communities, while also reviewing the social discount rate in light of recent interest-rate conditions.",""],[1,"40","5","Strategic Review of Disaster Prevention and Critical Infrastructure","When reviewing fields such as disaster prevention, science and technology, and critical infrastructure, the perspectives of maintaining national functions, maintaining supply capacity, and strategic autonomy will be emphasized in addition to cost-benefit analysis.",""]],"181":[[1,"38","7","Local General Revenue Securing Mechanism","Secure the total amount of local general revenues.",""],[1,"38","7","Public Procurement Price Pass-Through Measures","Through efforts such as passing on price increases in government procurement, realize a strong regional economy.",""],[1,"38","7","Sustainable Local Fiscal Governance Strengthening","Secure and strengthen the sustainability of the local public finance and administrative foundation supporting this.",""],[1,"38","7","Less Geographically Uneven Local Tax System","Take concrete measures toward constructing a local tax system with less geographic concentration, in line with the FY2026 ruling parties' tax reform outline.",""],[1,"38","9","Stable General Revenue Provision for Local Governments","Ensure, in substance, that the total amount of general revenues necessary for stable fiscal management by local governments, including grant-recipient local governments, does not fall below the level of the FY2026 Local Fiscal Plan.",""],[1,"39","1","Metropolitan Administrative System Review","Examine administrative systems and other matters in metropolitan areas.",""],[1,"39","1","Intergovernmental and Regional Cooperation Strengthening","Strengthen cooperation among local governments and collaboration across wider regions.",""],[1,"36","5","Support for Fiscally Weaker Local Governments","Strengthen support for local governments with weak fiscal capacity.",""],[1,"42","3","Local Government Fiscal Support Measures","Necessary and sufficient local fiscal measures will be taken so that local fiscal management and smooth project implementation are not impeded.",""]],"182":[[1,"40","5","Society-Rooted Well-being KPI Setting","Efforts toward realizing well-being rooted in Japanese society, including setting KPIs in relevant basic plans, will be expanded.",""],[1,"40","5","International Well-being Policy Contribution and Communication","Contribute to and communicate in international discussions.",""],[1,"40","7","OECD Well-being World Forum Engagement Mechanism","Utilize opportunities such as the OECD Well-being World Forum scheduled to be held in Japan in Reiwa 10.",""],[1,"35","3","Universal Health Coverage Knowledge Hub Initiative","Work toward realizing universal health coverage (UHC) through UHC knowledge hubs established in Japan.",""],[1,"35","3","International Infectious Disease and Health Systems Strengthening","Work on international infectious disease measures and strengthening health systems in cooperation with CEPI and the GHIT Fund.",""],[1,"35","3","International Expansion of Health and Care Services","Promote international expansion related to health, prevention, medical care, and nursing care.",""]],"183":[[1,"29","6","Responsible Proactive Fiscal Policy and Responsive Budgeting","Under \"responsible proactive fiscal policy,\" shift from uniform restraint-oriented budget formulation in the deflation and low-growth era to budget formulation that accurately reflects rising prices and wages and is appropriate for strengthening economic growth and expanding the nominal size of the economy.",""],[1,"29","7","Government Procurement Price Pass-Through Policy","Thoroughly ensure appropriate price pass-through in government procurement.",""],[1,"29","7","Officially Set Prices Support for Essential Services","For officially set prices in medical care, nursing care, childcare, welfare and other services, advance the measures necessary to secure personnel on the front lines, stabilize management, and ensure service quality.",""],[1,"29","7","Budget and Tax Threshold Review","Promote the necessary review and revision of various standard amounts and thresholds in budgets and the tax system, taking into account price and wage increases and changes in the socioeconomic environment.",""],[1,"41","5","Agile Execution of the Supplementary Budget","The FY2026 supplementary budget, compiled to provide a thorough response from the perspective of minimizing risks, will be executed appropriately and agilely in response to changes in circumstances.",""],[1,"41","5","Agile Economic Impact Monitoring and Response","The impacts on Japan's economy and prices will continue to be analyzed, and sufficient agile measures will be taken without hesitation to protect people's lives and business activities.",""],[1,"41","6","Stable Price Monetary Policy Operation","The Bank of Japan is expected to closely coordinate with the government and conduct appropriate monetary policy operations toward the sustainable and stable achievement of the 2 percent price stability target, while confirming a virtuous cycle between wages and prices.",""],[1,"41","8","Inflation-Responsive Public Budgeting and Unit Price Revision","In budget requests, the blanket restraint approach will be reviewed, and price and wage increases will be accurately reflected so that the level of administrative services can be maintained in real terms.",""],[1,"42","1","Publicly Regulated Service Pricing Measures","Appropriate measures will be taken in publicly regulated prices for medical care, nursing care, childcare, and welfare services.",""]],"184":[[1,"35","1","Menopausal Women’s Healthcare Promotion","Promote medical care for women in the menopausal generation.",""],[1,"35","1","Women’s Comprehensive Health Center Strengthening","Strengthen the functions of women’s comprehensive health centers.",""],[1,"35","1","Preconception Care Promotion Five-Year Plan","Formulate and implement a roadmap for the “Preconception Care Promotion Five-Year Plan.”",""],[1,"35","1","Corporate-Insurer Collaborative Health Promotion","Promote collaboration between companies and health insurers.",""],[1,"35","1","Health Management and Sleep Measures","Promote health management, including measures addressing sleep.",""],[1,"35","1","Healthcare Industry Development for Prevention","Develop the healthcare industry that supports prevention and health promotion.",""],[1,"35","5","Childhood Preventive Healthcare Programme","Includes a perspective of continuous preventive healthcare from childhood.",""],[1,"35","5","Oral Frailty Prevention and Management","Includes measures to address oral frailty and related issues.",""],[1,"35","5","Home-Visit Rehabilitation Service Expansion","Includes the enhancement of effective home-visit rehabilitation.",""],[1,"35","5","Five-Year Preconception Care Plan","A five-year plan was decided for the provision of preconception care.",""],[1,"35","5","Transport-Industry Sleep Apnea Measures","Further efforts will be made on measures addressing sleep apnea in the transport industry.",""],[1,"35","5","Sleep Disorder Medical Access Improvement","Further efforts will be made to improve access to medical care for sleep disorders.",""],[1,"35","5","Sleep Research Promotion","Further efforts will be made to promote sleep research.",""],[1,"35","5","Sleep Health Guide Dissemination","Further efforts will be made to disseminate and raise awareness of sleep guides.",""],[1,"35","5","Sleep Data Evidence-Building Support","Support will be provided for building evidence to create services using sleep and other data.",""],[1,"35","5","Sleep-Related Market and Business Support","Further efforts will also be made to expand sleep-related markets and support companies.",""],[1,"35","5","Integrative Medicine Research and Awareness","Includes research on and public awareness of so-called integrative medicine.",""],[1,"35","5","Sex-Difference Health Action Programme","Initiatives will be promoted based on the organization of issues concerning healthcare related to sex differences.",""],[1,"35","5","Expanded Pre-Treatment Cancer Gene Panel Testing","Includes expanding opportunities to receive cancer gene panel testing, currently provided as advanced medical care, before the start of standard treatment.",""]],"185":[[1,"35","5","Infectious Disease Epidemic Countermeasures Innovation Coalition","Infectious Disease Epidemic Countermeasures Innovation Coalition.",""],[1,"35","5","Global Health Innovative Technology Fund","Global Health Innovative Technology Fund.",""]],"186":[[1,"42","5","Basic Budget Formulation Policy Revision","In the latter half of the year, the basic policy for budget formulation will be revised as necessary, taking into account the status of its reflection in the FY2027 budget and changes in socioeconomic conditions, including the economic outlook.",""],[1,"42","6","Results-Based Budget Formulation and Improvement","After formulating the FY Reiwa 9 budget through this new budget-formulation approach, further improvements will be considered based on its results.",""]]}});